WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.889
"How Not to Die Documentary"

00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:29.600
There's an emerging
consensus that what's good

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.760
for our hearts is also good for our heads

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.880
because clogging of
arteries inside the brain

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.560
with atherosclerotic plaque is thought

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.840
to play a role in the
development of Alzheimer's.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.120
This is what our cerebral
arteries should look like.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.480
Open, clean, allowing blood
to flow throughout our brain.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:59.120
This is what atherosclerosis
in our head looks like.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.280
Clogged with cholesterol,
closing off arteries,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.720
clamping down on blood flow.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:13.265
What kind of brain arteries
do you want in your head?

00:01:13.265 --> 00:01:13.280
(intense music)

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.600
As dementia is one of our
greatest public health problems

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.400
and the most feared
condition of later life,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.600
there's kind of misconception

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.440
that we have no control over

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.040
whether or not we develop dementia.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.040
But the good news is that

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.400
although Alzheimer's may be incurable,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.000
at least it is preventable.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.720
Too much cholesterol in our blood

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.880
is unanimously recognized
to be a risk factor

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.183
for the development of
Alzheimer's disease.

00:01:45.183 --> 00:01:45.198
(intense music)

00:01:45.198 --> 00:01:47.360
- According to the Global
Burden of Disease study,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.440
our largest study of risk
factors is in human history.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.200
The number one cause of
death in the United States

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.400
is the American diet.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.800
Number one killer of men and women,

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.280
bumping tobacco smoking to number two.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.440
Tobacco now only kills about
500,000 Americans every year,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.640
whereas our diet kills many more.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.040
So it's the number one cause of death.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.440
Then obviously it's the number one thing

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.760
your doctor talks to you about, right?

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.200
Obviously it's the number one thing.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.640
I mean, you know, but no.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.680
- It's so dismal to have patients come in

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.360
with these reversible diseases

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.480
and just tell the patient,

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.120
"Oh, well I just have to
increase your statin dose

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.560
and come back in a month.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.040
At that point you're an
enabler of their disease.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.120
- Why do we have the
medical system we have,

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.960
which I consider to be flawed?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.800
A lot of good people working
in that community, obviously,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.200
but they're corrupted by a paradigm

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.160
that's been hanging over our
heads for more than a century.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.360
- We're trained to use drugs in surgery.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.120
We're reimbursed to use drugs in surgery,

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.720
so we use drugs in surgery.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:53.840
Abraham Maslow once said,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.280
if the only tool you have is a hammer,

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.560
you tend to see everything as a nail.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.720
And I think there's a
lot of truth to that.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.880
- If we could get people
to eat to save their heart,

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.720
it would markedly diminish the likelihood

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.680
of acquiring these common
Western cancers of breast,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.800
prostate, colon, and pancreatic.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.480
- So many times I have patients who come

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.640
and tell me, their doctor said,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.160
"Your inflammatory bowel disease

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:17.680
has nothing to do with nutrition.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:18.400
Don't worry about it.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.880
You just get medications
and you're gonna be fine."

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.423
You couldn't be farther from
the truth if you think that.

00:03:25.423 --> 00:03:25.438
(intense music)

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:28.560
- This is an investment
in your future self,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.720
that future self may be six months.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.240
That future self may be a
year, it may be 10 years.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.640
There is so much value in that

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.920
because we all can say,
"I don't mind dying."

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.760
It's not about dying.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.080
It's about are you
shortening that health span

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.680
and now you're sitting there
for five years, 10 years,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.720
12 years, a shell of yourself.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.280
You can neither live nor die.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.320
Who wants to live that life?

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:59.200
- I am a surgeon, a bariatric surgeon,

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.280
so I operate on obesity

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.240
and I also am boarded in
medical management of obesity.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.920
So I do both surgery and medical
management for weight loss.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.360
Funny enough, as a doctor,

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.560
you would think I would know better,

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.600
but I had no training in
nutrition as a doctor.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.320
Even in my training in
weight loss surgery,

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.640
I had no training in diet as a doctor.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.880
In fact, as a weight loss surgeon,

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.760
we kind of felt like
diets just don't work.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.000
- Allow me to begin

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.040
on a personal note.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.200
This is a picture of me
taken around the time

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.440
that my grandmother was diagnosed

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:48.400
with end stage heart disease
and sent home to die.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.720
(intense music)

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.800
The killer I'm talking about
is coronary heart disease.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.600
Plaque accumulates inside
the coronary arteries,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.160
the blood vessels that crown the heart,

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.760
and it's affecting nearly everyone

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:12.448
raised on the standard American diet.

00:05:12.448 --> 00:05:12.480
(waves whooshing)
(heart beating)

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.640
At that time, the medical
profession didn't even think

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.600
it was possible to reverse heart disease.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.720
Drugs were given to try
to slow the progression

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.240
and surgery was performed to
circumvent clogged arteries

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.480
to try to relieve symptoms.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.680
But the disease was expected to get worse

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.426
and worse until you die.

00:05:35.426 --> 00:05:37.280
(upbeat music)
She already had so many bypass surgeries,

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.360
basically run outta
plumbing at some point,

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.280
confined in a wheelchair,
crushing chest pain.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.120
There was nothing more they could do.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:46.880
Her life was over at age 65.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.995
(upbeat music)

00:05:50.995 --> 00:05:55.991
(waves whooshing)

00:05:55.991 --> 00:06:00.400
(intense music)

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.840
I think what sparks many kids

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.840
to wanna become doctors when they grow up

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:07.600
is watching a beloved relative
become ill or even die.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.400
But for me, who's watching
my grandma get better.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.320
Eventually I heard about
this guy, Nathan Pritikin,

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.000
one of our early lifestyle
medicine pioneers,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.240
and what happened next
is actually detailed

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.520
in Pritikin's biography.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.120
My grandma was one of
the death's door people.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.520
Francis Greger, my grandmother
arrived in wheelchair.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.920
Mrs. Greger had heart
disease, and claudication.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.600
Her condition so bad
she can no longer walk.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.400
- Heart disease is the
nation's number one killer.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.400
It accounts for half of all the deaths

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.000
in the United States.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.600
This year, more than 1 million
Americans will die from it.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:47.280
One reason almost all doctors
agree is the way we eat.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.800
Nathan Pritikin is not a
doctor, not even a nutritionist.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:54.240
Pritikin discovered he had heart
disease, which he reversed,

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.560
he says, by changing his diet.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.600
Would you say flatly

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.960
that you can reverse
serious heart disease?

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.840
- I would say that we can take

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.760
the most serious heart disease

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.320
and return them in many
cases to normal function.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.400
- We found we could reverse heart disease

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.600
in just three weeks.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.440
When you make really healthy changes,

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.120
most people feel so much
better so quickly, it reframes

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.520
the reason for making these
changes from fear of dying,

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.840
which is not sustainable,
to joy and pleasure

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.440
and love and feeling good, which are.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:25.200
- The normal American diet,
is so toxic to the body

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.360
that practically no human can stand up

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.040
against that kind of assault.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.000
In fact, almost anyone over
20 years old in this country,

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.480
I can almost guarantee
you by autopsy studies

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.480
has some closed arteries already.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.800
- 20
- 20, right.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:44.000
- Atherosclerosis, harden of the arteries,

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.800
is a disease that begins in childhood.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.200
By age 10, nearly all kids

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.800
raised on the standard
American diet already

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:55.520
have fatty streak building
up inside of their arteries

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.760
the first stage of the disease.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:01.360
These streaks then turn
into plaques in our 20s,

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.480
get worse in our 30s,

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.520
and then can start killing us off.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.040
In our heart causes a heart attack,

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.040
in our brain, the same disease
process causes a stroke.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.040
So if there is anyone here this morning,

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:20.701
older than age 10,

00:08:20.701 --> 00:08:20.720
(audience laughing)

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.880
then the question is not
whether or not to eat healthy

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.240
to prevent heart disease.

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:26.960
It's whether you wanna
reverse the heart disease

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:32.400
you likely already have,
whether you know it or not.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.480
But is that even possible?

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.200
You know, when researchers
took people with heart disease,

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.960
put them on the kind of plant-based diet,

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.000
followed by populations

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.080
that do not get epidemic heart disease,

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.640
their hope was maybe we
could slow the disease down

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:48.800
a little bit, maybe even stop it.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:54.320
Instead, something miraculous happened.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:58.160
As soon as people stopped
eating an artery clogging diet,

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:01.040
their bodies were able to start
dissolving that plaque away,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.760
opening up art without
drugs, without surgery,

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:07.760
suggesting their bodies wanted
to be healthy all along,

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.360
but we're just never given the chance.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.160
This remarkable improvement
in the blood flow

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.840
to the heart muscle itself

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:22.225
was after just three weeks
of plant-based nutrition.

00:09:22.225 --> 00:09:27.920
(intense music)
Imagine if terrorists created a bio agent

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.680
that spread mercilessly claiming the lives

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:33.680
of nearly 400,000 Americans every year.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.520
We'd marshaled the army,

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:38.240
march in our finest
medical minds into the room

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:41.120
to figure out a cure for
this bio-terror plague.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.960
In short, we'd stop at nothing

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.600
until the terrorists were stopped.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.480
This particular biological
weapon may not be a germ

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.440
released by terrorists,

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.080
but it kills more Americans annually

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.680
than have all our past wars combined.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.360
It can be stopped, not in a laboratory,

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.480
but right in our grocery stores,

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:06.320
kitchens, and dining rooms.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:11.983
As far as weapons go, we don't
need vaccines or antibiotics.

00:10:11.983 --> 00:10:14.480
(water whooshing)
A simple fork will do.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.680
(intense music)

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:20.000
Nathan Pritikin gaining a reputation

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.720
for reversing terminal heart disease,

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.640
opened a new center in California,

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.120
and my grandmother in desperation

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.280
somehow made the cross country trek

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:31.440
to become one of his first patients.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.880
This was a live-in program

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:35.040
where everyone was placed
on a plant-based diet

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.320
and then started on a
graded exercised regimen.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.760
Within three weeks though,

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.520
not only was she out of her wheelchair,

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:43.760
she was walking 10 miles a day.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.680
Here's a picture of my grandma

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.520
15 years after doctors
had abandoned her to die.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:52.000
Though she was giving her
medical death senses at age 65,

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.760
thanks to a healthy diet,

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.480
was able to enjoy another
31 years on this planet

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:00.480
till age 96 to continue to
enjoy our six grandkids,

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:01.840
including me.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:08.080
That's why I went into medicine.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:11.027
(intense music)
(audience cheering)

00:11:11.027 --> 00:11:13.920
- I remember her going out to Pritikin,

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:18.480
she came back and she was overly...

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:22.240
She'd look at the bread
that I had and said,

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:25.760
"What? This has oil in
it, or it has souls in it.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.040
Or it has this in it,

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.400
and you're killing everybody."

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:34.080
You see, we lived near her

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.840
when we were living in
Florida temporarily.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:51.120
Yeah, she lived to 96.
- 96.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.720
(intense music)
A plant-based nutrition appears

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:58.400
to be the principle
component, alone accounting

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.800
for about half the difference in lifespan.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:05.680
No wonder since the number
one risk factor for death

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.840
in the United States

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:12.560
is the American diet.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:19.200
Now, if you can read here,
you know, unsafe sex, bad.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:24.880
Sedentary lifestyle, bad.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:30.400
Alcohol and drugs,
particularly tobacco, bad,

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:31.840
but cigarettes now only kill

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.680
about a half million Americans every year,

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:38.400
whereas our diet kills many more.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:42.240
We are what we eat, which is good news

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:46.080
because it means we have the power.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:49.040
We're talking about life and death here.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.080
You go online and you hear,
you know, people spouting,

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.560
you know, nutritional
nonsense with some, you know,

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.960
corrupting commercial
influencers or something.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:00.720
And it's not like someone
is lying to you to get you

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.400
to buy their brand of toothpaste.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.080
But when someone says, you know,

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:06.800
"Here, eat this bacon and butter diet,"

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.000
we're talking about people
that could die over this.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.600
These are life and death decisions.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.600
Remember diet number one cause.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.840
If there was any decision

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:20.000
to be made in life based on evidence,

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.240
it should be what to feed
ourselves and our family.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.640
It's the most important decision

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:26.640
as to how long we and our loved ones live.

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:30.080
- It makes me want to apologize
to patients everywhere

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.480
for the practitioners of my profession,

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:36.000
who, I have to be charitable here,

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.640
but we're not taught
anything about nutrition.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.640
Most doctors don't respect nutrition,

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:43.360
even though they're seeing
nutrition based diseases all day

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:45.280
in their clinic, and they're eating

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:46.720
the same foods themselves.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.200
They're eating the burgers and
the pizzas and the lobsters

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:49.840
and the steaks,

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.160
they're not gonna tell
their patients don't eat it.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:55.440
- When you hear all the
diets that are out there,

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.200
there's only one that I'm aware of

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.680
that has ever taken patients
who are seriously ill

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:04.640
with heart disease and
be able to get a halting

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:09.360
of the disease and
reversal of the disease.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.560
And that's whole food,
plant-based nutrition.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:17.360
It doesn't happen with paleo,
it doesn't happen with keto,

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:20.480
doesn't happen with Atkins,
doesn't happen with Agatston

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.640
or Barry Sears or you know,

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:25.120
these are all caring physicians,

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:28.960
but when the research is
done, it's whole food,

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:30.320
plant-based nutrition,

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.360
it will halt and reverse heart disease.

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:38.240
- In this country, when
doctors are trained,

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:40.480
there's not a medical
school in the United States

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.560
that teaches nutrition.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.640
- We published a paper
recently where we surveyed

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:49.200
how much nutrition training
does the average doctor get

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.960
in four years of medical school?

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.760
And it turns out it's
about four hours a year.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.920
You know, and even then
it's really about, you know,

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.000
vitamin C and scurvy and vitamin B

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.840
and beri-beri, things like that.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.200
And then we looked at the average amount

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:04.240
of training in nutrition the
average cardiologist gets

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:07.580
in four years of fellowship
training, and it's a zero.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:11.680
- Time and again, is so
apparent they had very little

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.080
information whatsoever about nutrition,

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:17.680
either in medical school or in
their postgraduate training.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.680
- We have in this country, for example,

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.640
about 130 different medical specialties.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:24.560
And those medical specialties,

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:27.200
they document their
experience with a patient.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:30.800
And so it turns out that
all 130 medical specialties,

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:32.400
there's not one called nutrition.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.720
- We're talking about
life and death situations.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.400
We need to stop eating animal products

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:39.920
with high saturated fat, high
sugar, refined carbohydrates.

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:42.320
If we do all that, which
would be a whole food,

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.880
plant-based diet, and
we're doing the exercise,

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.880
we're paying attention to
our weight, blood pressure,

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.800
cholesterol, no one smoking.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:51.240
We can actually do this. It's not hard.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:54.560
- So does the American Heart Association

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:55.920
recommend a no meat?

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:59.040
No, they recommend this low meat diet,

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.480
the so-called DASH diet.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:04.400
So wait a second, when this
DASH diet was being created,

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.840
I mean, were they just not aware

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:10.160
of this landmark research
done by Harvard's Frank Sacks?

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.000
No, they were aware.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.560
The chair of the design
committee that came up

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:18.400
with the DASH diet was Frank Sacks.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:22.400
See the Dash diet was created to try

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.960
to get the benefits of eating
a more plant-based diet,

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:31.680
yet contain enough animal
products to make it palatable

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.000
to the general population.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:38.080
They didn't think the public
could handle the truth.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:42.000
Now, I mean, in their
defense, you can kind of see

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.200
what they were thinking, right?

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:46.800
Just like drugs never work

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.280
unless you actually take them.

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:52.720
Diets never work at all
unless you actually eat them.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:53.760
So they're like, look how many people

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:55.760
are gonna eat strictly plant-based, right?

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:58.160
If we soft pedal the message,

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.480
come up with some kind
of compromised diet,

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:03.200
well then on a population scale,

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.600
we might do more good.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:09.280
Okay, tell that

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:13.200
to the thousand American families a day

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:18.080
that lose a loved one
to high blood pressure.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:22.240
Maybe it's time to start
telling the American public

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:28.320
the truth.

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:33.680
(audience clapping)

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:36.960
Which is that in the
United States of America,

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:41.280
most deaths are preventable
and related to nutrition.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:44.800
The number one cause of
death in these United States

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.840
is the American diet.

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:50.640
- When Western Medicine talks
about disease prevention,

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:52.320
they're really talking
about early diagnosis.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:54.480
They're not talking
about not getting sick,

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.240
they're talking about, let's catch it

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:57.440
when you first get sick.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:00.240
So there's colonoscopy
and there's mammogram,

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.720
and you know, lab tests like PSA

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.400
and things like that for prostate cancer.

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:05.920
So we're never telling someone,

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:08.240
"Hey, this is how you eat
to not get colon cancer,"

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:10.320
or, "This is how you eat to
not get prostate cancer."

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.720
Because really in the mind of a doctor,

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:14.240
they almost don't think of food

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.160
having anything to do with this.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.080
It's almost like disease is just bad luck.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:22.320
Like I really literally
thought that our bodies,

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:23.920
it was almost like, you
know, how you get a car,

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:26.640
you call it a lemon 'cause it's
a bad car, it's gonna break.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.080
That's what I saw the human body as.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.320
I mean, it's gonna break
down and I'm a fix it guy

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:32.160
and I'm gonna fix it up with my tools

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:34.240
and you stay outta the way.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:36.400
Let me do my job and you'll be fine.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:38.320
I switched onto a more plant-based diet.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:40.000
I thank God there were
a few doctors out there

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:43.280
that had written some papers
and I started doing research

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:45.120
and the more research I did, I was like,

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:48.640
oh my God, it is the food that we eat

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:52.320
and it's the exact
opposite of what I'm eating

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:53.360
and what I'm telling patients.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.440
And then of course I start
looking around my patients.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:56.960
Everybody's got the same diseases

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.240
and they're not separate diseases.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.360
We think of them separately.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.520
We think there's obesity
and there's heart disease

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:04.320
and there's cancer and there's diabetes.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:05.840
They're all one disease process.

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:08.240
I mean, they're all part
of an inflammatory process.

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:13.760
- How can there be this
disconnect between the science

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:16.480
and the practice of mainstream medicine?

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:22.000
Well, let's do a little
thought experiment.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:28.720
Imagine yourself a
smoker back in the 1950s.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:32.080
The average per capita
cigarette consumption,

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:39.105
4,000 cigarettes a year.

00:19:39.105 --> 00:19:42.160
(intense music)
The media was telling people to smoke.

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:44.160
Famous athletes agreed,

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:48.640
even Santa Claus wanted you to smoke.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.320
(audience laughing)

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:53.520
I mean, look, you wanna keep fit

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.840
and stay trimmed so you make sure to smoke

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:59.680
and eat lots of hot dogs to stay trim

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:02.240
and you eat lots of sugar to stay slim

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:04.400
and trim a lot better
than that apple there.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.720
I mean, shees, right?

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:11.040
Hey, but "Apples do connote
goodness and freshness,"

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.360
reads one internal tobacco industry memo,

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:16.080
which brings up "many possibilities
for a youth-oriented."

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.240
They wanna make apple flavored cigarettes

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:21.520
