00:21:00.305 --> 00:21:00.320
(intense music)

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:04.640
You know, back then even the
paleo folks were smoking.

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:06.480
And so were the doctors.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:09.440
Now, this is not to say
there wasn't controversy

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:10.960
within the medical profession.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.920
I'm sure you know, some
doctors smoke Camels,

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:16.000
but others preferred Lucky.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.320
So there was a little disagreement there.

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:21.360
The leader of the US Senate agreed,

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:25.200
who wouldn't want to give
their throat a vacation?

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:28.160
Not a single case of throat irritation.

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:32.640
How could there be when
"Cigarettes are just as pure

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.040
as the water you drink?"

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:38.160
But anyway, if your throat
does get a little irritated,

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:41.040
don't worry because your
doctor can always write you

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:44.000
a prescription for cigarettes.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:44.400
This is in

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.600
the "Journal of the American
Medical Association."

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:50.640
So when the AMA is on record saying

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:55.200
that smoking on balance
may be good for you,

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.120
where could you turn back then

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.440
if you just wanted the science?

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:02.800
I mean, what's the new
data advanced by science?

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:06.800
Well, she was, "Too tired for fun

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:10.381
and then she smoked a camel."

00:22:10.381 --> 00:22:10.400
(audience laughing)

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:13.600
Babe Ruth spoke of proof
positive medical science

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:16.240
that is when he still could speak

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:20.960
before he died of throat cancer.

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:23.920
If by some miracle back then

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:27.520
there was some kinda
smokingfacts.org website

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:30.560
that could have delivered
the science directly,

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:33.680
bypassing commercially
corruptible institutional filters,

00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:36.240
you would've become aware
of studies like this.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:38.400
There's an Adventist
study outta California

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:41.120
published in 1958 showing that non-smokers

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:44.640
had at least 90% less
lung cancer than smokers.

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:46.640
But this wasn't the first.

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:48.800
When famed surgeon Michael DeBakey

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:51.280
was asked why his studies back in the '30s

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:52.720
linking lung cancer and smoking

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:56.080
were simply ignored off
the face of the planet,

00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:58.880
he had to remind people
what it was like back then.

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:01.440
We were a smoking society.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:03.120
It was in the movies on airplanes,

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:05.440
medical meetings were
one heavy haze of smoke.

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:10.945
Smoking was, in a word, normal.

00:23:10.945 --> 00:23:14.400
(intense music)
So back to our thought experiment.

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:19.120
Imagine you're a smoker
in the '50s in the know.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:20.480
What do you do?

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:22.800
I mean, with access to the science,

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.880
you realize the best
available balance of evidence

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:28.160
suggest your smoking habits,
ah, not so good for you.

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:31.200
So do you change or do you wait?

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:33.280
If you wait until your doctor tells you

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:38.400
between puffs to quit,
you'd have cancer by then.

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:39.920
If you wait until the powers that be

00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:41.120
officially recognized it,

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:44.640
like the Surgeon General did
in the subsequent decade,

00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:46.400
you could be dead by then.

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:48.960
It took more than 25 years,

00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:52.800
it took more than 7,000 studies

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:54.400
and the deaths of countless smokers

00:23:54.400 --> 00:23:56.000
before the first Surgeon General

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.840
report against smoking came out.

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:01.200
You'd think maybe after
the first 6,000 studies

00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:05.760
could give people little
heads up or something.

00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:08.400
Powerful industry.

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:10.000
Maybe we should have stopped smoking

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:15.440
after the 700th study like this came out.

00:24:15.440 --> 00:24:17.920
But as a smoker in the
'50s, on one hand you had

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:20.960
all of society, the government,

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:24.880
the medical profession
itself telling you to smoke.

00:24:24.880 --> 00:24:29.840
And on the other hand, all
you had was the science.

00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:32.640
If you're even aware of studies like this.

00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:34.480
Let's fast forward 55 years.

00:24:34.480 --> 00:24:36.880
You know, there's a new
Adventist study outta California

00:24:36.880 --> 00:24:39.040
warning Americans about something else

00:24:39.040 --> 00:24:41.360
they may be putting in their mouths.

00:24:41.360 --> 00:24:42.720
Of course, it's not just one study,

00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:44.240
put all the studies together

00:24:44.240 --> 00:24:46.720
and deaths from all causes put together,

00:24:46.720 --> 00:24:48.480
including many of our dreaded diseases,

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:51.200
stroke, cancer, significantly lower

00:24:51.200 --> 00:24:54.560
among those eating more plant-based diets.

00:24:54.560 --> 00:24:57.920
So instead of someone going along

00:24:57.920 --> 00:25:00.560
with America's smoking habits in the '50s,

00:25:00.560 --> 00:25:02.960
imagine you or someone you know

00:25:02.960 --> 00:25:08.640
going along with America's
eating habits today,

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:10.160
what do you do?

00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:12.800
I mean, with access to the science,

00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:15.200
you realize the best available
balance of evidence is yes,

00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:17.760
you're eating habitant
not so good for you.

00:25:17.760 --> 00:25:21.040
So do you change or do you wait?

00:25:21.040 --> 00:25:24.640
I mean, if you wait until
your doctor tells you

00:25:24.640 --> 00:25:28.800
between bites to quit,
it could be too late.

00:25:28.800 --> 00:25:31.920
In fact, even after the Surgeon
General's report came out,

00:25:31.920 --> 00:25:34.800
the American Medical Association
officially went on record

00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:37.280
refusing to endorse it, why?

00:25:37.280 --> 00:25:37.920
Could it have been

00:25:37.920 --> 00:25:40.240
because they were just
handed a $10 million check

00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:43.760
from the tobacco industry, maybe.

00:25:43.760 --> 00:25:46.160
Okay, so we can see why
the AMA was sucking up

00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:47.360
to the tobacco industry,

00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:50.160
but why weren't more
individual doctors speaking up?

00:25:50.160 --> 00:25:52.080
There were a few, ahead of their time,

00:25:52.080 --> 00:25:55.120
speaking up against
industries killing millions.

00:25:55.120 --> 00:25:56.880
But why not more?

00:25:56.880 --> 00:25:59.280
Maybe it's because

00:25:59.280 --> 00:26:05.680
the majority of physicians
themselves smoked cigarettes.

00:26:05.680 --> 00:26:08.800
Just like the majority of physicians today

00:26:08.800 --> 00:26:10.640
continue to eat foods
that are contributing

00:26:10.640 --> 00:26:12.960
to our epidemics of dietary disease.

00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:15.680
What was the AMAs rallying cry back then?

00:26:15.680 --> 00:26:18.080
Everything in moderation.

00:26:18.080 --> 00:26:21.840
Extensive scientific studies,
proven smoking in moderation.

00:26:21.840 --> 00:26:25.840
Oh, that's fine.

00:26:25.840 --> 00:26:27.520
Sound familiar?

00:26:27.520 --> 00:26:31.200
- If you cut out the animal protein

00:26:31.200 --> 00:26:32.720
and the animal fat,

00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:36.080
which has in the literature clearly proven

00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:40.720
to cause gut disease, if you
cut this junk outta your diet,

00:26:40.720 --> 00:26:42.360
you are gonna be healthier.

00:26:42.360 --> 00:26:43.920
- Why do I say it's a little bit better?

00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:46.080
Well, if I look at historical data,

00:26:46.080 --> 00:26:48.720
it tells us that animal
protein versus plant protein,

00:26:48.720 --> 00:26:50.560
plant protein wins.

00:26:50.560 --> 00:26:53.320
So if this is a plant
protein, it's going to win.

00:26:53.320 --> 00:26:55.920
- One of the quotes that I
really love is from Wendell Berry

00:26:55.920 --> 00:26:58.720
who said, "The problem that
we have is that, you know,

00:26:58.720 --> 00:27:02.000
we've got a food care system
that doesn't care about health

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:04.320
and a healthcare system that
doesn't care about food."

00:27:04.320 --> 00:27:08.240
And that's how we get into
the problem that we're in.

00:27:08.240 --> 00:27:09.440
(intense music)

