to downplay the risk of candy.

00:27:28.240 --> 00:27:30.400
And the same paid for by the meat industry

00:27:30.400 --> 00:27:32.720
to downplay the risks of meat.

00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:35.040
Whereas processed foods and animal foods

00:27:35.040 --> 00:27:43.280
we're talking 14 million
lives lost every year.

00:27:43.280 --> 00:27:46.080
So those of us involved in
this evidence-based nutrition

00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:50.160
revolution, we're talking
about 14 million lives

00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:51.840
in the balance.

00:27:51.840 --> 00:27:54.320
So plant-based eating can be considered

00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:57.360
kind of the modern day
nutritional equivalent

00:27:57.360 --> 00:27:58.960
of stopping smoking.

00:27:58.960 --> 00:28:02.080
But how long do we have to
wait before the CDC says,

00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:04.240
"Don't wait for open heart surgery

00:28:04.240 --> 00:28:08.720
before starting to eat
healthier," as well.

00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:11.200
Until society changes,

00:28:11.200 --> 00:28:14.400
we need to take personal
responsibility for our own health,

00:28:14.400 --> 00:28:15.680
for our family's health.

00:28:15.680 --> 00:28:19.920
We can't wait until society
catches up to the science again

00:28:19.920 --> 00:28:24.640
because it's a matter of life and death.

00:28:24.640 --> 00:28:27.280
The science was there since the 1930s.

00:28:27.280 --> 00:28:30.800
We've known that tobacco
associated with lung cancer,

00:28:30.800 --> 00:28:33.520
yet it took literally decades

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:35.360
before the powers that be

00:28:35.360 --> 00:28:37.280
have actually came out and said it.

00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:39.120
We are in the same situation today.

00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:42.640
We have this mount of
evidence implicating our diet

00:28:42.640 --> 00:28:45.360
as the leading killer of men
and women in the United States,

00:28:45.360 --> 00:28:48.480
yet we're still not seeing
pronouncements from on high,

00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:50.880
just the acknowledgement
of the available science.

00:28:50.880 --> 00:28:53.200
So that means we have
to take our own health,

00:28:53.200 --> 00:28:54.960
the our own family's health,

00:28:54.960 --> 00:28:58.320
we have to take a responsibility for it

00:28:58.320 --> 00:29:01.040
until we finally get

00:29:01.040 --> 00:29:03.520
that acknowledgement of the science.

00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:06.080
It's gonna be a while before
we can see warning labels

00:29:06.080 --> 00:29:08.720
before ads on TV saying don't wait

00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:11.520
until the cancer diagnosis
before you stop smoking.

00:29:11.520 --> 00:29:12.720
The same thing with diet.

00:29:12.720 --> 00:29:14.720
And so we're just in that window.

00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:18.640
We're in that transition period
where the science is there

00:29:18.640 --> 00:29:20.080
for anyone to see,

00:29:20.080 --> 00:29:23.200
but it's just kind of
hidden upon public view.

00:29:23.200 --> 00:29:25.360
And so we just need to get it out there.

00:29:25.360 --> 00:29:28.400
- And because these underlying
biological mechanisms

00:29:28.400 --> 00:29:30.080
are so dynamic, you know,

00:29:30.080 --> 00:29:31.920
and so for someone who, you know,

00:29:31.920 --> 00:29:34.880
gets 30 or 40 episodes
of chest pain a day,

00:29:34.880 --> 00:29:37.120
can't walk across the street
without getting chest pain

00:29:37.120 --> 00:29:39.440
or make love with their spouse
or play with their kids,

00:29:39.440 --> 00:29:42.240
or go back to work without
having angen or chest pain,

00:29:42.240 --> 00:29:43.440
and usually within a few weeks

00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:45.700
they're essentially pain free.

00:29:45.700 --> 00:29:48.880
- That's been my whole life,
is to get the word out.

00:29:48.880 --> 00:29:52.480
The good news that we
have tremendous power

00:29:52.480 --> 00:29:54.880
over our health destiny and longevity.

00:29:54.880 --> 00:29:57.120
The vast majority of
premature death and disability

00:29:57.120 --> 00:29:59.440
is preventable with a plant-based diet

00:29:59.440 --> 00:30:02.000
and other healthy lifestyle behaviors.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:11.120
- Michael, you know, he was
always very independent.

00:30:11.120 --> 00:30:13.920
You know, he never talked about it,

00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:17.920
but he just decided he was
not going to eat meat anymore.

00:30:18.880 --> 00:30:21.520
He's a good kid.

00:30:21.520 --> 00:30:25.920
He spent two years, he
just went from one place

00:30:25.920 --> 00:30:28.560
to another giving lectures.

00:30:28.560 --> 00:30:30.560
He didn't have a place to live.

00:30:30.560 --> 00:30:34.960
He'd stay in somebody's
couch or something.

00:30:34.960 --> 00:30:41.259
He got to know a lot of people.

00:30:41.259 --> 00:30:42.960
(audience clapping)
- So when Dr. Dean Ornish published

00:30:42.960 --> 00:30:44.880
his landmark lifestyle heart trial,

00:30:44.880 --> 00:30:47.360
proving with something called
quantitative angiography

00:30:47.360 --> 00:30:49.840
that indeed heart disease
could be reversed,

00:30:49.840 --> 00:30:52.240
arteries opened up without
drugs, without surgery,

00:30:52.240 --> 00:30:53.680
just a plant-based diet

00:30:53.680 --> 00:30:55.440
and other healthy lifestyle behaviors,

00:30:55.440 --> 00:30:58.720
I assumed this was gonna
be the game changer.

00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:02.320
1990 when Dr. Dean Ornish's
lifestyle heart trial came out,

00:31:02.320 --> 00:31:04.400
that was the turning
point personally for me

00:31:04.400 --> 00:31:07.120
and should have been the turning
point for all of medicine.

00:31:07.120 --> 00:31:08.960
I mean, my family had seen
it with their own eyes,

00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:11.040
but here it was in black and white

00:31:11.040 --> 00:31:13.440
published some of the most
prestigious medical journals

00:31:13.440 --> 00:31:17.680
in the world, yet nothing happened.

00:31:17.680 --> 00:31:20.240
Remember, there's this
hidden mountain of evidence.

00:31:20.240 --> 00:31:23.180
It's not hidden in the literature,
the medical literature,

00:31:23.180 --> 00:31:25.760
it's there for anyone to
go to a medical library

00:31:25.760 --> 00:31:27.920
and down into the dusty
stacks of the basement

00:31:27.920 --> 00:31:29.040
to pull it out.

00:31:29.040 --> 00:31:33.200
It's like those 6,000 tobacco
studies, right? Just here.

00:31:33.200 --> 00:31:35.120
Look, if you would still wanna smoke,

00:31:35.120 --> 00:31:37.040
it's your body, your choice.

00:31:37.040 --> 00:31:39.200
Smoke, go bungee jump,

00:31:39.200 --> 00:31:41.600
disconnect all the smoke
alarms in your house,

00:31:41.600 --> 00:31:43.680
whatever you want to do,
whatever floats your boat.

00:31:43.680 --> 00:31:47.920
But just know the predictable
consequences of your actions.

00:31:47.920 --> 00:31:51.120
I said wait a second,
if effectively the cure

00:31:51.120 --> 00:31:52.800
to our number one killer could get lost

00:31:52.800 --> 00:31:54.240
down some rabbit hole and ignored,

00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:56.160
what else might there be
in the medical literature

00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:57.440
that could help my patients

00:31:57.440 --> 00:31:59.200
but just didn't have a corporate budget

00:31:59.200 --> 00:32:00.240
driving its promotion?

00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:04.080
Well, I made it my life's
mission to find out.

00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:06.800
For those of you unfamiliar
with my work, every year I read

00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:08.560
through every issue of
every English language

00:32:08.560 --> 00:32:09.840
nutrition journal in the world

00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:14.560
so busy folks like you don't have to.

00:32:14.560 --> 00:32:16.320
(audience laughing)
And then compile all the most interesting,

00:32:16.320 --> 00:32:18.000
most groundbreaking,
most practical findings

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:20.320
to new videos and articles
that I upload every day

00:32:20.320 --> 00:32:29.421
to my non-profit site, nutritionfacts.org.

00:32:29.421 --> 00:32:31.120
(audience cheering)
Everything on the website is free.

00:32:31.120 --> 00:32:33.040
There's no ads, no corporate sponsorship,

00:32:33.040 --> 00:32:35.440
strictly non-commercial, not
selling anything, no kickbacks.

00:32:35.440 --> 00:32:41.263
We just put it up as a
tribute to my grandmother.

00:32:41.263 --> 00:32:43.040
(intense music)
- If everyone ate the way I ate

00:32:43.040 --> 00:32:44.960
or the way I tell patients to eat,

00:32:44.960 --> 00:32:47.440
I'd somewhat be out of business.

00:32:47.440 --> 00:32:49.120
If people ate like that, yeah,

00:32:49.120 --> 00:32:52.160
it would be a humongous
change in healthcare.

00:32:52.160 --> 00:32:54.640
It would be very preventative
to a vast majority

00:32:54.640 --> 00:32:56.080
of the diseases that we have

00:32:56.080 --> 00:32:59.280
because that diet is
taking out meat and dairy,

00:32:59.280 --> 00:33:01.360
which we know from epidemiology,

00:33:01.360 --> 00:33:03.120
we know from randomized controlled trials,

00:33:03.120 --> 00:33:04.880
we know from looking at societies

00:33:04.880 --> 00:33:08.960
that live long healthy
lives like the blue zones,

00:33:08.960 --> 00:33:10.800
that stuff is bad for you.

00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:14.800
And so really what's left
is this just life affirming,

00:33:14.800 --> 00:33:17.840
life giving fruits,
vegetables, antioxidants,

00:33:17.840 --> 00:33:22.560
phytonutrients fiber that
fosters a perfect microbiome.

00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:24.960
Yeah, that would just eliminate disease

00:33:24.960 --> 00:33:27.280
or vastly reduce it.

00:33:27.280 --> 00:33:28.720
The actual doctors

00:33:28.720 --> 00:33:32.080
from the Dietary Guidelines
Advisory Committee,

00:33:32.080 --> 00:33:34.000
they say eat less meat.

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:35.600
They say eat more fruits and vegetables.

00:33:35.600 --> 00:33:39.600
If you look at the plate that
the government recommends,

00:33:39.600 --> 00:33:41.440
it's a quarter fruit,
a quarter vegetables,

00:33:41.440 --> 00:33:45.840
a quarter grains, and then
it's say a quarter protein.

00:33:45.840 --> 00:33:47.440
But if you then go and look

00:33:47.440 --> 00:33:49.360
at where our tax dollars are spent,

00:33:49.360 --> 00:33:51.200
are they spent a quarter on fruits,

00:33:51.200 --> 00:33:52.560
a quarter on vegetables?

00:33:52.560 --> 00:33:53.440
No, not at all.

00:33:53.440 --> 00:33:56.480
It's spent mainly on meat
and dairy and grains,

00:33:56.480 --> 00:33:59.840
but most of that grains to
go to feed meat and dairy.

00:33:59.840 --> 00:34:01.760
So I think it's important
for the government

00:34:01.760 --> 00:34:06.240
to do something, but you could
see where there's a problem

00:34:06.240 --> 00:34:07.600
with the government doing anything

00:34:07.600 --> 00:34:12.000
as long as we allow
lobbyists to drive policy,

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:14.520
which we do in our current system.

00:34:14.520 --> 00:34:18.800
- So where did Pritikin
get his evidence from?

00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:21.120
Well, you know, a network of
missionary hospitals set up

00:34:21.120 --> 00:34:23.840
throughout Sub-Saharan
Africa uncovered what may be

00:34:23.840 --> 00:34:26.080
one of the most important
advances in health.

00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:28.560
The fact that many of our major diseases

00:34:28.560 --> 00:34:32.560
were universally rare, like heart disease.

00:34:32.560 --> 00:34:34.720
The African population
of Uganda, for example,

00:34:34.720 --> 00:34:36.880
coronary artery disease,
was almost non-existent.

00:34:36.880 --> 00:34:39.920
You say, wait a second, our
number one cause of death,

00:34:39.920 --> 00:34:41.200
almost non-existent.

00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:42.720
What were they eating?

00:34:42.720 --> 00:34:46.320
Well, they we're eating lots
of vegetables and grains

00:34:46.320 --> 00:34:48.880
and greens and their
protein almost entirely

00:34:48.880 --> 00:34:50.880
from plant sources.

00:34:50.880 --> 00:34:54.160
And they had the cholesterol
levels to prove it.

00:34:54.160 --> 00:35:06.945
Very similar to what we see
in modern day plant eaters.

00:35:06.945 --> 00:35:07.920
(intense music)
So wait a second,

00:35:07.920 --> 00:35:10.080
maybe they were just dying
early from something else.

00:35:10.080 --> 00:35:12.880
Never lived long enough
to get heart disease. No.

00:35:12.880 --> 00:35:15.760
Here's age match heart
attack rates in Uganda

00:35:15.760 --> 00:35:17.920
versus St. Louis.

00:35:17.920 --> 00:35:20.640
Now 632 autopsies in Uganda,

00:35:20.640 --> 00:35:23.280
only one myocardial infarction.

00:35:23.280 --> 00:35:27.760
Outta 632 age and gender match autopsies

00:35:27.760 --> 00:35:30.960
in Missouri, 136 myocardial infarctions.

00:35:30.960 --> 00:35:32.720
More than a hundred times the rate

00:35:32.720 --> 00:35:34.080
of our leading killer.

00:35:34.080 --> 00:35:36.000
In fact, they were so
blown away, went back,

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.920
did another 800 autopsies.

00:35:37.920 --> 00:35:41.280
Ugandan still just that
one small healed infarct,

00:35:41.280 --> 00:35:43.040
meaning it wasn't even the cause of death.

00:35:43.040 --> 00:35:48.960
Out of 1,427 patients, less
than one in a thousand.

00:35:48.960 --> 00:35:55.804
Whereas here, heart
disease is an epidemic.

00:35:55.804 --> 00:35:55.838
(intense music)
(audience clapping)

00:35:55.838 --> 00:35:58.960
- He got arrested a couple of times.

00:35:58.960 --> 00:36:04.000
In fact, in his medical school book,

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:06.880
everybody has a page of the graduates

00:36:06.880 --> 00:36:10.000
and everybody has a picture
of them and their wives

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:15.040
or children and that
Michael had his mugshot.

00:36:15.040 --> 00:36:17.120
(intense music)

00:36:17.120 --> 00:36:20.160
This was when he was in medical school

00:36:20.160 --> 00:36:23.600
and he got arrested several times.

00:36:23.600 --> 00:36:27.360
- Following the footsteps of my parents

00:36:27.360 --> 00:36:29.760
who were arrested over and over

00:36:29.760 --> 00:36:31.680
during the civil rights movement,

00:36:31.680 --> 00:36:33.600
in between classes at med school,

00:36:33.600 --> 00:36:35.600
I would go feed people on the commons

00:36:35.600 --> 00:36:37.440
with the organization Food Not Bombs,

00:36:37.440 --> 00:36:39.840
which was technically illegal

00:36:39.840 --> 00:36:41.920
and helped move homeless families

00:36:41.920 --> 00:36:45.520
into empty city-owned housing
units with Homes Not Jails.

00:36:45.520 --> 00:36:48.560
All my arrests were for civil disobedience

00:36:48.560 --> 00:36:52.320
upholding Article 25 of the
UN Declaration of Human Rights

00:36:52.320 --> 00:36:55.120
that everyone has a right
to a standard of living,

00:36:55.120 --> 00:36:56.960
adequate for the health
and wellbeing of themselves

00:36:56.960 --> 00:37:00.080
and their family,
including food, clothing,

00:37:00.080 --> 00:37:11.920
housing, and medical care.

00:37:11.920 --> 00:37:12.000
(intense music)
(audience clapping)

00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:16.320
With enough portion control,
anyone can lose weight.

00:37:16.320 --> 00:37:17.760
Lock someone in a closet,

00:37:17.760 --> 00:37:19.920
you can force them to lose
as much body fat as you want.

00:37:19.920 --> 00:37:23.200
Chaining them to what treadmill
would've a similar effect.

00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:26.080
But what's the most
effective weight loss regime

00:37:26.080 --> 00:37:28.960
that doesn't involve caloric restriction

00:37:28.960 --> 00:37:31.360
or exercise or a felony?

00:37:31.360 --> 00:37:35.920
Well, I have scoured

00:37:35.920 --> 00:37:37.280
through the medical literature

00:37:37.280 --> 00:37:39.760
and all the randomized controlled trials.

00:37:39.760 --> 00:37:42.800
And the single most
successful strategy to date

00:37:42.800 --> 00:37:45.440
is a diet of whole plant foods.

00:37:45.440 --> 00:37:47.920
The single most effective
weight loss intervention

00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:49.120
like that ever published

00:37:49.120 --> 00:37:50.720
in the peer reviewed
scientific literature,

00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:54.960
a whole food plant-based diet.

00:37:54.960 --> 00:37:56.480
(intense music)

00:37:56.480 --> 00:37:59.840
The most frustrating thing
about being a physician

00:37:59.840 --> 00:38:01.840
in primary care

00:38:01.840 --> 00:38:05.360
is our patients don't get better.

00:38:05.360 --> 00:38:08.560
About 80% of what a
primary care physician sees

00:38:08.560 --> 00:38:10.880
in their practice are things
like type two diabetes,

00:38:10.880 --> 00:38:12.560
obesity, high blood pressure,

00:38:12.560 --> 00:38:15.440
things that just get worse,
worse, worse then you die.

00:38:15.440 --> 00:38:19.200
And so what physicians can
do is prescribe medications

00:38:19.200 --> 00:38:22.960
to try to slow down the rate
at which their diabetics

00:38:22.960 --> 00:38:26.080
go blind, at which their
diabetics go on dialysis

00:38:26.080 --> 00:38:27.920
or lose their lower limbs.

00:38:27.920 --> 00:38:31.840
Because they're not treating
the underlying cause,

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:36.480
all they're doing is kind
of trying to slow the rate

00:38:36.480 --> 00:38:40.640
of the demise of their patient.

00:38:40.640 --> 00:38:43.120
That's why lifestyle
medicine is so important.

00:38:43.120 --> 00:38:45.680
If we can treat the underlying
cause, we can prevent arrest

00:38:45.680 --> 00:38:48.480
and even reverse some
of the chronic diseases

00:38:48.480 --> 00:38:53.743
that are decimating our population.

00:38:53.743 --> 00:38:55.040
(intense music)
- Every one of us physicians

00:38:55.040 --> 00:38:57.040
who practices a lifestyle medicine

00:38:57.040 --> 00:39:00.080
and gets our patients on
whole food, plant-based diets,

00:39:00.080 --> 00:39:03.360
we witness this remarkable transformation,

00:39:03.360 --> 00:39:06.640
this kind of food stream
flowing through the body,

00:39:06.640 --> 00:39:09.200
meal after meal, week after week,

00:39:09.200 --> 00:39:12.720
produces wonderful
effects that within days

00:39:12.720 --> 00:39:16.320
the obesity starts to melt
away and the arteries open up

00:39:16.320 --> 00:39:18.320
and the high blood pressure comes down

00:39:18.320 --> 00:39:20.000
and the joints stop hurting.

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:23.360
And the asthmatic lungs
stop wheezing so much,

00:39:23.360 --> 00:39:25.600
the migraine headaches get better

00:39:25.600 --> 00:39:29.040
and people turn into
normal healthy people,

00:39:29.040 --> 00:39:32.080
normal heights and normal
weights and blood pressures

00:39:32.080 --> 00:39:33.840
and they don't need a lot of pills

00:39:33.840 --> 00:39:35.120
and potions and procedures.

00:39:35.120 --> 00:39:38.480
- We're all the same when
it comes to eating food.

00:39:38.480 --> 00:39:42.160
We can maintain ethnic cuisines
of course using the flavors

00:39:42.160 --> 00:39:44.240
and spices and herbs and stuff like that.

00:39:44.240 --> 00:39:47.040
But we should be eating quite frankly,

00:39:47.040 --> 00:39:49.280
whole plant-based foods.

00:39:49.280 --> 00:39:53.920
We're looking at a solution
for creating health

00:39:53.920 --> 00:39:56.560
unlike anything we've ever seen before.

00:39:56.560 --> 00:40:00.080
- Surely if there was some safe,

00:40:00.080 --> 00:40:04.560
simple side effect-free solution
to the obesity epidemic,

00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:06.880
we would know about it by now, right?

00:40:06.880 --> 00:40:08.560
I'm not so sure.

00:40:08.560 --> 00:40:11.760
It may take an average of 17 years

00:40:11.760 --> 00:40:14.400
before research evidence makes it

00:40:14.400 --> 00:40:16.720
in day-to-day clinical practice.

00:40:16.720 --> 00:40:17.760
To take one example

00:40:17.760 --> 00:40:21.040
that was particularly
poignant for me and my family,

00:40:21.040 --> 00:40:22.560
heart disease.

00:40:22.560 --> 00:40:25.840
Decades ago Dr. Dean
Ornish published evidence

00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:28.880
in one of the most prestigious
medical journals in the world

00:40:28.880 --> 00:40:33.680
that our leading cause of
death could be reversed

00:40:33.680 --> 00:40:36.080
with diet and lifestyle changes alone.

00:40:36.080 --> 00:40:38.480
Yet hardly anything changed.

00:40:38.480 --> 00:40:41.600
Even now, hundreds of
thousands of Americans

00:40:41.600 --> 00:40:44.320
continue to needlessly die every year

00:40:44.320 --> 00:40:46.560
from what we learned decades ago

00:40:46.560 --> 00:40:50.640
was a potentially reversible condition.

00:40:50.640 --> 00:40:56.943
I had seen it with my own eyes.

00:40:56.943 --> 00:40:59.040
(intense music)
- These are choices that people make.

00:40:59.040 --> 00:41:00.480
I always used to say that, you know,

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:04.000
the coronary heart disease
is culinary heart disease

00:41:04.000 --> 00:41:06.320
mispronouncing it on purpose, okay?

00:41:06.320 --> 00:41:11.185
And saying that it's an elbow problem.

00:41:11.185 --> 00:41:11.200
(intense music)

00:41:11.200 --> 00:41:12.960
When the patient's in
the coronary care unit,

00:41:12.960 --> 00:41:13.920
I'm usually seeing them

00:41:13.920 --> 00:41:15.520
'cause I'm not doing invasive cardiology,

00:41:15.520 --> 00:41:17.120
I'm seeing them on
rounds the next morning.

00:41:17.120 --> 00:41:20.640
Okay, so I say "I'm gonna
ask you to do a little quiz

00:41:20.640 --> 00:41:23.520
with me just to tell me

00:41:23.520 --> 00:41:25.680
where you are in terms of your thinking.

00:41:25.680 --> 00:41:27.200
And I'm gonna ask you some questions

00:41:27.200 --> 00:41:30.080
and they sound a little silly,
but you have just humor me

00:41:30.080 --> 00:41:32.320
and let's see how far
we can get with this.

00:41:32.320 --> 00:41:34.640
Tell me what happened to
you while you're here."

00:41:34.640 --> 00:41:36.800
And I say, "I had a heart attack."

00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:40.320
"That's right, how did
the heart attack happen?"

00:41:40.320 --> 00:41:42.400
"Well, they told me I
had a blocked artery."

00:41:42.400 --> 00:41:48.000
"That's right. What was it
blocked with?" "Plaque."

00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:50.800
"That's right. What's plaque made out of?"

00:41:51.520 --> 00:41:53.600
"Fat and cholesterol."

00:41:53.600 --> 00:41:54.880
"That's exactly right.

00:41:54.880 --> 00:41:58.160
And where did that fat and
cholesterol come from?"

00:41:58.160 --> 00:42:03.040
The patient says 100%
of the time, "I ate it"

00:42:03.040 --> 00:42:03.840
(intense music)

00:42:03.840 --> 00:42:06.560
- [Michael] Back in 1903,

00:42:06.560 --> 00:42:09.520
Thomas Edison predicted that
the doctor of the future

00:42:09.520 --> 00:42:10.480
will give no medicine

00:42:10.480 --> 00:42:12.400
but will instruct his patient in the care

00:42:12.400 --> 00:42:15.040
of the human frame in
diet and in the cause

00:42:15.040 --> 00:42:17.760
and prevention of diseases.

00:42:17.760 --> 00:42:22.851
Edison's prediction hasn't come true.

00:42:22.851 --> 00:42:22.866
(intense music)

00:42:22.866 --> 00:42:26.320
- [Announcer] Why don't
we give a big warm welcome

00:42:26.320 --> 00:42:31.680
to Dr. Michael Greger.

00:42:31.680 --> 00:42:34.648
(audience cheering)

00:42:34.648 --> 00:42:37.920
- You know, some people are
overwhelmed by medical articles

00:42:37.920 --> 00:42:42.400
and research and you know,
having a way for somebody to,

00:42:42.400 --> 00:42:44.480
you know, disseminate
that information to you,

00:42:44.480 --> 00:42:46.560
I think is paramount.

00:42:46.560 --> 00:42:48.320
I'm a cancer survivor.

00:42:48.320 --> 00:42:50.320
I became a vegetarian shortly

00:42:50.320 --> 00:42:52.480
after going through my treatments.

00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:54.720
It's been about 15 years now.

00:42:54.720 --> 00:42:56.960
I was learning a lot from the things

00:42:56.960 --> 00:42:58.800
that Dr. Greger was publishing.

00:42:58.800 --> 00:43:00.880
There's a lot of mixed
messaging out there about

00:43:00.880 --> 00:43:03.440
what you should be eating
and what you should be doing.

00:43:03.440 --> 00:43:05.520
One of the things I do
appreciate about Nutrition Facts

00:43:05.520 --> 00:43:08.640
is it does make a lot of
the harder information

00:43:08.640 --> 00:43:09.680
easier to consume.

00:43:09.680 --> 00:43:11.600
I think his videos are engaging.

00:43:11.600 --> 00:43:14.240
His personality is amazing.

00:43:14.240 --> 00:43:17.880
If you aren't laughing,
I don't know what to say.

00:43:17.880 --> 00:43:21.360
- The notion that a
calorie from one source

00:43:21.360 --> 00:43:24.960
is just as fattening as any
other is a trope broadcast

00:43:24.960 --> 00:43:27.200
by the food industry as
a way to absolve itself

00:43:27.200 --> 00:43:28.560
of culpability.

00:43:28.560 --> 00:43:31.600
Coca-Cola itself even put an ad out there

00:43:31.600 --> 00:43:36.240
emphasizing this "one
simple common-sense fact."

00:43:36.240 --> 00:43:38.320
As the current and past chairs

00:43:38.320 --> 00:43:41.120
of the Harvard's Nutrition
Department put it,

00:43:41.120 --> 00:43:43.120
"This central argument from industry

00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:45.520
is that the overconsumption of calories

00:43:45.520 --> 00:43:48.160
from carrots would be no different

00:43:48.160 --> 00:43:52.160
than the overconsumption
of calories from soda."

00:43:52.160 --> 00:43:54.960
If a calorie's just a
calorie, why does it matter

00:43:54.960 --> 00:44:00.480
what we put in our mouth?

00:44:00.480 --> 00:44:02.440
(intense music)

00:44:02.440 --> 00:44:04.400
(opera singing)

00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:08.480
It is true that in a tightly
controlled laboratory setting,

00:44:08.480 --> 00:44:10.320
240 calories of carrots

00:44:10.320 --> 00:44:12.080
would have the same
effect on calorie balance

00:44:12.080 --> 00:44:18.467
than the 240 calories in a bottle of Coke.

00:44:18.467 --> 00:44:21.840
(opera music)
But this comparison falls flat on its face

00:44:21.840 --> 00:44:23.440
out in the real world.

00:44:23.440 --> 00:44:26.560
You could chug those liquid candy calories

00:44:26.560 --> 00:44:28.720
in less than a minute.

00:44:28.720 --> 00:44:32.000
But eating 240 calories of carrots

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:34.800
would take you more than
two and a half hours

00:44:34.800 --> 00:44:42.368
of sustained, constant chewing.

00:44:42.368 --> 00:44:42.400
(audience laughing)
(opera music)

00:44:42.400 --> 00:44:46.640
Not only would your jaw get sore,

00:44:46.640 --> 00:44:52.160
but 240 calories of
carrots is like five cups.

00:44:52.160 --> 00:44:55.680
You might not even be
able to fit them all in.

00:44:55.680 --> 00:45:01.320
In a lab, a calorie is a
calorie, but in life far from it.

00:45:01.320 --> 00:45:05.840
- Unfortunately, if you go to
your doctor, the doctor says,

00:45:05.840 --> 00:45:08.000
"Take these pills to
lower your blood pressure

00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:10.000
or your cholesterol or your blood sugar."

00:45:10.000 --> 00:45:12.000
And they say, "Doctor, how
long do I have to take these?"

00:45:12.000 --> 00:45:14.000
The doctor, he says, "Forever."

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:15.280
And the reason is that the pill

00:45:15.280 --> 00:45:18.080
doesn't make you feel better,
but the lifestyle changes do.

00:45:18.080 --> 00:45:20.160
And there's no point in giving
up something that you enjoy

00:45:20.160 --> 00:45:22.800
unless you get something back
that's better and quickly.

00:45:22.800 --> 00:45:25.200
And because these underlying
biological mechanisms

00:45:25.200 --> 00:45:28.960
are so dynamic, when you
make really healthy changes,

00:45:28.960 --> 00:45:31.600
eat well, move more,
stress less, love more,

00:45:31.600 --> 00:45:34.640
most people feel so
much better so quickly.

00:45:34.640 --> 00:45:36.880
It reframes the reason
for making these changes

00:45:36.880 --> 00:45:39.120
from fear of dying,
which is not sustainable,

00:45:39.120 --> 00:45:41.600
to joy and pleasure and love
and feeling good, which are.

00:45:41.600 --> 00:45:45.840
- What amazing potential
the body has to heal itself.

00:45:45.840 --> 00:45:48.080
I, as a physician have a lot to do

00:45:48.080 --> 00:45:49.760
educating my colleagues.

00:45:49.760 --> 00:45:52.480
Before you order another $1,000 scan,

00:45:52.480 --> 00:45:54.960
another $500 set of blood tests,

00:45:54.960 --> 00:45:57.200
ask your patient what they ate yesterday.

00:45:57.200 --> 00:45:59.520
And if it's full of
burgers and buffalo wings,

00:45:59.520 --> 00:46:01.040
then that's where to start.

00:46:01.040 --> 00:46:03.840
Send the patient to a plant-based
dietician down the hall.

00:46:03.840 --> 00:46:06.280
Take them shopping and
stock their refrigerator up.

00:46:06.280 --> 00:46:10.160
- Medical education practice
is funded by big pharma,

00:46:10.160 --> 00:46:14.160
both in undergraduate and
postgraduate medical education.

00:46:14.160 --> 00:46:16.480
I've never been offered to
been taken out to dinner

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:17.520
by big broccoli.

00:46:17.520 --> 00:46:19.280
There's a reason for that.

00:46:20.080 --> 00:46:23.200
These are the cash cow
drugs for big pharma.

00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:25.040
Give a drug for a lifestyle condition,

00:46:25.040 --> 00:46:26.480
that means you have to take
the drug every single day

00:46:26.480 --> 00:46:27.840
for the rest of your life.

00:46:27.840 --> 00:46:29.120
That's where the money is.

00:46:29.120 --> 00:46:31.760
New blood pressure pill, new
cholesterol lowering pill.

00:46:31.760 --> 00:46:33.120
And that's their bread and butter.

00:46:33.120 --> 00:46:35.520
And here we come along
and say, "Wait a second.

00:46:35.520 --> 00:46:37.680
No, no, we can lower your cholesterol

00:46:37.680 --> 00:46:39.200
as much, if not better.

00:46:39.200 --> 00:46:42.000
Have all these positive,
healthy side effects

00:46:42.000 --> 00:46:44.000
with diet and lifestyle."

00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:47.160
Yet it's just not as
profitable for big pharma.

00:46:47.160 --> 00:46:50.480
- We really cannot
underestimate the public.

00:46:50.480 --> 00:46:54.080
When you think back on it,

00:46:54.080 --> 00:46:59.200
it took over 7,000 scientific papers

00:46:59.200 --> 00:47:02.080
to finally get the Surgeon General to say

00:47:02.080 --> 00:47:05.600
that smoking was harmful to your health.

00:47:05.600 --> 00:47:08.240
Now since that has happened,

00:47:08.240 --> 00:47:09.760
the amount of smokers have gone

00:47:09.760 --> 00:47:14.160
from 40 million to 20 million.

00:47:14.160 --> 00:47:15.430
(intense music)

00:47:15.430 --> 00:47:18.560
- We really try to change
the outcome of our patients

00:47:18.560 --> 00:47:21.600
by not just the modern
guideline-driven management

00:47:21.600 --> 00:47:25.040
of medications and revascularizations
the latest therapies

00:47:25.040 --> 00:47:27.600
that you can do with
this device for that one.

00:47:27.600 --> 00:47:30.960
But really changing the,
what we like to say,

00:47:30.960 --> 00:47:33.200
changing the paradigm by
turning off the faucet

00:47:33.200 --> 00:47:39.200
instead of mopping up the floor.

00:47:39.200 --> 00:47:46.409
(intense music)
(water bubbling)

00:47:46.409 --> 00:47:49.200
- [Michael]

00:47:49.200 --> 00:47:51.120
Drug companies are
more than happy to sell you

00:47:51.120 --> 00:47:52.960
a new roll of paper towels every day

00:47:52.960 --> 00:47:54.080
for the rest of your life

00:47:54.080 --> 00:47:57.280
while the water continues to gush.

00:47:57.280 --> 00:48:00.640
- A hundred years in a row
that cardiovascular disease

00:48:00.640 --> 00:48:02.480
is the leading killer of Americans.

00:48:02.480 --> 00:48:04.720
It's time that we actually
start really turning

00:48:04.720 --> 00:48:07.520
off the faucet instead of
just mopping up the floor.

00:48:07.520 --> 00:48:10.240
- Is it really true

00:48:10.240 --> 00:48:14.880
that protein might increase cancer risk?

00:48:14.880 --> 00:48:16.880
And so being a biochemist as I am,

00:48:16.880 --> 00:48:20.880
we had an opportunity also
of not only determining

00:48:20.880 --> 00:48:25.920
whether that's true, but if
it is true, how does it work?

00:48:25.920 --> 00:48:29.680
So we spent many of those
years at first showing

00:48:29.680 --> 00:48:31.280
that yes, it is true.

00:48:31.280 --> 00:48:32.720
When I say yes, it is true,

00:48:32.720 --> 00:48:35.920
I mean, when animals are fed
higher levels of protein,

00:48:35.920 --> 00:48:38.800
animal protein, they get cancer.

00:48:38.800 --> 00:48:43.120
But at lower levels they don't.

00:48:43.120 --> 00:48:44.880
And one of the key
experiments that we did,

00:48:44.880 --> 00:48:48.400
I found very, very exciting
was that we could turn on

00:48:48.400 --> 00:48:51.600
and turn off cancer
growth just by adjusting

00:48:51.600 --> 00:49:00.385
the level of the protein, animal protein.

00:49:00.385 --> 00:49:00.400
(intense music)

00:49:00.400 --> 00:49:04.720
That was very exciting
for some various reasons.

00:49:04.720 --> 00:49:08.480
One of which is the idea
now recognized these days

00:49:08.480 --> 00:49:15.745
at least by me, that we can
control cancer by nutrition.

00:49:15.745 --> 00:49:15.760
(intense music)

00:49:15.760 --> 00:49:18.080
The second thing related
to that was the idea

00:49:18.080 --> 00:49:20.640
that we could actually reverse cancer

00:49:20.640 --> 00:49:23.080
'cause that's what we did.

00:49:23.080 --> 00:49:27.200
- Let me share with you what's been called

00:49:27.200 --> 00:49:31.440
the best kept secret in all of medicine.

00:49:31.440 --> 00:49:32.960
The best kept secret in medicine

00:49:32.960 --> 00:49:36.000
is that sometimes given
the right conditions,

00:49:36.000 --> 00:49:41.520
the body can sometimes heal itself.

00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:43.360
You know, if you, you know,

00:49:43.360 --> 00:49:45.600
whack your shin really hard
in a coffee table, right?

00:49:45.600 --> 00:49:47.600
Get a red hot, painful, swollen, inflamed,

00:49:47.600 --> 00:49:50.480
but will heal naturally if you stand back,

00:49:50.480 --> 00:49:52.640
let your body work it's magic.

00:49:52.640 --> 00:49:56.080
Okay, what if you hit
yourself in the same place

00:49:56.080 --> 00:49:59.280
day after day or three times
a day, breakfast, lunch

00:49:59.280 --> 00:50:02.400
and dinner, you'd never heal.

00:50:02.400 --> 00:50:03.520
You'd go to your doctor, you'd be like,

00:50:03.520 --> 00:50:04.480
"Ah, my shin hurts."

00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:05.440
They'd be like, "No problem."

00:50:05.440 --> 00:50:06.320
Whip out their pad.

00:50:06.320 --> 00:50:09.680
Write your prescription
for it, pain killers.

00:50:09.680 --> 00:50:11.520
You're still whacking your
sin three times a day.

00:50:11.520 --> 00:50:12.720
Still really hurts like heck,

00:50:12.720 --> 00:50:17.040
but oh, feel so much better
with those pain pills on board.

00:50:17.040 --> 00:50:20.701
Thank heavens for modern medicine.

00:50:20.701 --> 00:50:20.720
(audience laughing)

00:50:20.720 --> 00:50:26.160
Our body wants to come back
to health if we let it.

00:50:26.160 --> 00:50:29.600
But if we keep reinjuring
ourselves, keep stabbing ourselves

00:50:29.600 --> 00:50:34.080
with a fork three times
a day, we may never heal.

00:50:34.080 --> 00:50:35.920
You know, one of the most
amazing things I learned

00:50:35.920 --> 00:50:37.680
in all my medical training

00:50:37.680 --> 00:50:40.000
was that within 15 years
of stopping smoking,

00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:41.360
your lung cancer rates approach

00:50:41.360 --> 00:50:43.600
that of a lifelong non-smoker.

00:50:43.600 --> 00:50:44.720
Isn't that amazing?

00:50:44.720 --> 00:50:46.960
Like your lungs can clear out all that tar

00:50:46.960 --> 00:50:49.360
and eventually, it's almost

00:50:49.360 --> 00:50:51.600
as if you never started smoking at all.

00:50:51.600 --> 00:50:53.920
Where our body wants
to come back to health.

00:50:53.920 --> 00:50:56.640
And so every morning of our smoking life,

00:50:56.640 --> 00:50:59.680
that healing process starts until wham

00:50:59.680 --> 00:51:01.680
first cigarette of the day.

00:51:01.680 --> 00:51:03.520
Reinjuring our lungs with every puff,

00:51:03.520 --> 00:51:05.440
just like we can reinjure our arteries

00:51:05.440 --> 00:51:06.560
with every bite.

00:51:06.560 --> 00:51:08.480
When all we had to do all along,

00:51:08.480 --> 00:51:13.120
the miracle cure is just stand back,

00:51:13.120 --> 00:51:16.480
get out of the way, stop
re-damaging ourselves

00:51:16.480 --> 00:51:18.960
and let our body's
natural healing processes

00:51:18.960 --> 00:51:22.320
bring us back towards health.

00:51:22.320 --> 00:51:26.480
Sure you can choose moderation

00:51:26.480 --> 00:51:31.501
and hit yourself with a smaller hammer,

00:51:31.501 --> 00:51:35.520
(audience laughing)
but why beat yourself up at all?

00:51:35.520 --> 00:51:39.040
We've known about this for decades.

00:51:39.040 --> 00:51:43.520
"American Heart Journal,"
1977 cases like Mr. F.W here,

00:51:43.520 --> 00:51:46.160
heart disease so bad,
couldn't even make it

00:51:46.160 --> 00:51:49.040
to the mailbox.

00:51:49.040 --> 00:51:51.600
Started eating healthier.

00:51:51.600 --> 00:51:56.057
Few months later, he was
climbing mountains, no pain.

00:51:56.057 --> 00:51:56.920
(audience laughing)
All right.

00:51:56.920 --> 00:52:01.440
- We really do like to
improve people's outcomes.

00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:05.920
And even though it may cost
us revenue in a given patient,

00:52:05.920 --> 00:52:07.120
because most of our people

00:52:07.120 --> 00:52:10.160
who follow their
medication do the exercise

00:52:10.160 --> 00:52:12.480
and do plant-based
nutrition, don't come back

00:52:12.480 --> 00:52:13.920
to the stress lab and they don't come back

00:52:13.920 --> 00:52:15.040
to the coronary care unit.

00:52:15.040 --> 00:52:17.920
And we're not making money
off of those people anymore.

00:52:17.920 --> 00:52:20.000
But it opens us up for new patients.

00:52:20.000 --> 00:52:21.520
And so, you know, the people

00:52:21.520 --> 00:52:24.960
who really are not following
the program, they're smoking,

00:52:24.960 --> 00:52:27.760
they're eating animal products,
high fat, high sodium,

00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:29.680
they're coming back in
and out of heart failure

00:52:29.680 --> 00:52:32.240
and hospital readmissions are a problem.

00:52:32.240 --> 00:52:35.040
But the people who
actually adopt lifestyle,

00:52:35.040 --> 00:52:36.560
we're moving their clinic visits out

00:52:36.560 --> 00:52:39.200
from six or 10 weeks to six to 10 months

00:52:39.200 --> 00:52:41.680
and seeing them sometimes once a year.

00:52:41.680 --> 00:52:44.800
And that actually does
give us access to try

00:52:44.800 --> 00:52:46.320
and help the community around us.

00:52:46.320 --> 00:52:48.720
We are in an area that's saturated

00:52:48.720 --> 00:52:51.840
with cardiovascular diseases,
a lot of Hispanic patients,

00:52:51.840 --> 00:52:53.360
a lot of African American patients,

00:52:53.360 --> 00:52:55.040
but really all varieties.

00:52:55.040 --> 00:52:56.880
The burden of cardiovascular disease

00:52:56.880 --> 00:52:58.640
is so great in around the country.

00:52:58.640 --> 00:53:00.320
- You know, if we wanted to make money,

00:53:00.320 --> 00:53:01.600
you go to the stock market or something,

00:53:01.600 --> 00:53:03.040
people go into medicine

00:53:03.040 --> 00:53:05.200
because they care about
people, yet we get in there

00:53:05.200 --> 00:53:06.960
and our patients don't get better.

00:53:06.960 --> 00:53:08.800
I've heard these stories so many times

00:53:08.800 --> 00:53:13.280
from my lifestyle medicine
colleagues that, you know,

00:53:13.280 --> 00:53:15.360
in the back of my mind I'm thinking,

00:53:16.080 --> 00:53:18.800
I've been telling you this,
like there's a mountain

00:53:18.800 --> 00:53:20.960
of peer reviewed medical evidence

00:53:20.960 --> 00:53:23.200
going back decades proving this.

00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:25.600
But no, it took the one anecdote,

00:53:25.600 --> 00:53:30.480
like the one person in front
of you to change your mind.

00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:34.560
Same with the risk of
cognitive impairment.

00:53:34.560 --> 00:53:37.440
Only healthy plant-based
diets reduce risks.

00:53:37.440 --> 00:53:41.840
Same with dementia and
depression. The same with frailty.

00:53:41.840 --> 00:53:47.440
Healthy, plant foods, good,
plant-based junk, bad.

00:53:47.440 --> 00:53:50.960
And the same with aging.

00:53:50.960 --> 00:53:54.560
The more people cut down
on meat, dairy, and eggs,

00:53:54.560 --> 00:53:56.400
the slower they appear to age.

00:53:56.400 --> 00:53:58.320
But that's only if they replace them

00:53:58.320 --> 00:53:59.520
with healthy plant foods.

00:53:59.520 --> 00:54:04.560
Pile on the junk and you
can accelerate aging.

00:54:04.560 --> 00:54:09.600
That's why Cornell professor
emeritus biochemistry,

00:54:09.600 --> 00:54:13.520
T. Colin Campbell coined
the term whole food,

00:54:13.520 --> 00:54:16.000
plant-based diet.

00:54:16.000 --> 00:54:20.000
- Reversing cancer by nutritional means,

00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:23.440
cancer being promoted
by animal-based protein,

00:54:23.440 --> 00:54:27.520
the most revered of all
nutrients for a century or two.

00:54:27.520 --> 00:54:30.080
- The more that
information gets out there,

00:54:30.080 --> 00:54:31.360
the more patients are gonna show up

00:54:31.360 --> 00:54:33.200
to their doctors getting healthier.

00:54:33.200 --> 00:54:34.560
And that's not what people do.

00:54:34.560 --> 00:54:36.880
People don't get healthier over time.

00:54:36.880 --> 00:54:39.360
And so when that happens,
that really opens the eyes.

00:54:39.360 --> 00:54:42.880
- And if we could just get
everybody to understand

00:54:42.880 --> 00:54:44.320
what is good nutrition.

00:54:44.320 --> 00:54:47.840
And that of course starts
not just with parenting,

00:54:47.840 --> 00:54:49.120
it starts with cardiologists.

00:54:49.120 --> 00:54:51.760
The leading cause of
death is of cardiologists,

00:54:51.760 --> 00:54:52.880
it's still heart disease.

00:54:53.680 --> 00:54:56.480
Plenty of people who get a
stent put in by a cardiologist

00:54:56.480 --> 00:54:58.960
and they're now told
nothing about their diet.

00:54:58.960 --> 00:55:00.160
And when I see that

00:55:00.160 --> 00:55:02.080
I don't just worry about the patient,

00:55:02.080 --> 00:55:03.840
I will worry about the provider.

00:55:03.840 --> 00:55:06.000
Because if they don't know
to tell the patient that,

00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:07.440
it's gonna get them.

00:55:07.440 --> 00:55:11.360
- As my good friend Kim Williams who said

00:55:11.360 --> 00:55:17.520
"There are two types of
cardiologists, those who are vegan

00:55:17.520 --> 00:55:22.048
and those who have not yet
read the literature." (laughs)

00:55:22.048 --> 00:55:24.800
- The sicker people are,
the more they spend money,

00:55:24.800 --> 00:55:26.640
the more they can charge for premiums.

00:55:26.640 --> 00:55:30.000
Again, these perverse incentives

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:34.400
where the less healthy people
are, the more money is made.

00:55:34.400 --> 00:55:38.960
I mean it's just an
unfortunate kind of consequence

00:55:38.960 --> 00:55:40.880
of our for-profit medical system.

00:55:40.880 --> 00:55:45.200
But again, we can step
back, stick with the signs

00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:50.320
and save ourselves and our families.

00:55:50.320 --> 00:55:56.480
(intense music)

00:55:56.480 --> 00:55:59.440
1930s, a group of diabetics

00:55:59.440 --> 00:56:02.960
placed on a plant-based diet
over a period of five years.

00:56:02.960 --> 00:56:06.560
A quarter of them were able
to get off insulin altogether.

00:56:06.560 --> 00:56:07.840
But plant-based diets

00:56:07.840 --> 00:56:10.640
tend to be relatively low calorie diets.

00:56:10.640 --> 00:56:14.080
I mean, maybe their diabetes got better

00:56:14.080 --> 00:56:17.760
just because they lost so much weight.

00:56:17.760 --> 00:56:19.840
To tease that out, what we'd have to do

00:56:19.840 --> 00:56:22.080
is put people on a plant-based diet

00:56:22.080 --> 00:56:24.400
but force them to eat so much food

00:56:24.400 --> 00:56:26.880
that they don't lose any weight.

00:56:26.880 --> 00:56:29.920
Then we can see if there's
some, you know, unique benefits

00:56:29.920 --> 00:56:32.560
to plant-based eating beyond
just all the easy weight loss.

00:56:32.560 --> 00:56:37.680
Well we'd have to wait
44 years, but here it is.

00:56:37.680 --> 00:56:40.400
Insulin needs were cut
60% across the board,

00:56:40.400 --> 00:56:43.280
half the diabetics ended off
all their insulin altogether.

00:56:43.280 --> 00:56:46.080
Wow, how many years did that take?

00:56:46.080 --> 00:56:50.480
No, 16 days.

00:56:50.480 --> 00:56:52.800
16 days later.

00:56:52.800 --> 00:56:55.840
So we're talking diabetics
who've had diabetes for 20 years,

00:56:55.840 --> 00:56:57.680
injecting 20 units of insulin a day

00:56:57.680 --> 00:57:00.240
and then 13 days later on, none.

00:57:00.240 --> 00:57:03.280
Diabetes for 20 years,

00:57:03.280 --> 00:57:06.880
then off all insulin
in less than two weeks.

00:57:06.880 --> 00:57:11.200
Diabetes for 20 years
'cause no one had told them

00:57:11.200 --> 00:57:14.640
about a plant-based diet.

00:57:14.640 --> 00:57:20.480
For decades, they were
13 days away at any time

00:57:20.480 --> 00:57:21.920
from being free.

00:57:21.920 --> 00:57:25.360
Lower blood sugars on
32 units less insulin.

00:57:25.360 --> 00:57:28.880
That's the power of plants.

00:57:28.880 --> 00:57:32.800
And as a bonus, cholesterol
drop like a rock

00:57:32.800 --> 00:57:36.080
to under 150 again in 16 days.

00:57:36.080 --> 00:57:39.120
So just like making
moderate changes in diet

00:57:39.120 --> 00:57:41.760
may only net you modest
reductions in cholesterol.

00:57:41.760 --> 00:57:46.400
How moderate do you want your diabetes?

00:57:46.400 --> 00:57:48.880
Asking diabetics to make
moderate changes in diet

00:57:48.880 --> 00:57:52.720
can leave them with moderate blindness,

00:57:52.720 --> 00:57:55.920
moderate kidney failure,
moderate amputate,

00:57:55.920 --> 00:57:59.261
maybe just a few toes or something.

00:57:59.261 --> 00:57:59.280
(audience laughing)

00:57:59.280 --> 00:58:04.160
Moderation in all things isn't
necessarily a good thing.

00:58:04.160 --> 00:58:06.800
You know, there's a famous
study published in a journal

00:58:06.800 --> 00:58:08.160
called "Cell Metabolism,"

00:58:08.160 --> 00:58:10.160
which purported to show
that diets high meat,

00:58:10.160 --> 00:58:12.720
eggs and dairy could be as
harmful to health as smoking.

00:58:12.720 --> 00:58:14.560
Explaining that for those in middle aged

00:58:14.560 --> 00:58:16.080
who eat a lot of meat, eggs, and dairy,

00:58:16.080 --> 00:58:22.400
four times as likely to
die from cancer, diabetes.

00:58:22.400 --> 00:58:24.560
But if you look at the actual study,

00:58:24.560 --> 00:58:27.040
you'll see that's simply not true.

00:58:27.040 --> 00:58:29.200
Those eating a lot of
animal protein in middle age

00:58:29.200 --> 00:58:32.400
didn't have four times the
risk of dying from diabetes

00:58:32.400 --> 00:58:36.560
they 73 times the risk
of dying from diabetes.

00:58:36.560 --> 00:58:39.680
Now those only eating a moderate
amount of animal protein,

00:58:39.680 --> 00:58:45.920
oh, they just had 23
times the risk of death.

00:58:45.920 --> 00:58:47.200
The academic institution

00:58:47.200 --> 00:58:49.760
where this study was done
sent out a press release

00:58:49.760 --> 00:58:53.840
with a memorable opening line,

00:58:53.840 --> 00:58:55.440
"That chicken wing you're eating

00:58:55.440 --> 00:59:00.160
could be as deadly as a cigarette."

00:59:00.160 --> 00:59:02.640
Eating lots of a diet
rich and animal protein

00:59:02.640 --> 00:59:06.080
four times as likely to die from cancer.

00:59:06.080 --> 00:59:07.120
I mean that's comparable

00:59:07.120 --> 00:59:09.360
to what one might get smoking, right?

00:59:09.360 --> 00:59:13.280
So I mean, what was the response
in the academic community

00:59:13.280 --> 00:59:15.280
to this revelation that diets high meat,

00:59:15.280 --> 00:59:17.600
eggs and dairy could be
harmful to health of smoking?

00:59:17.600 --> 00:59:20.560
Well, one nutrition scientist
said it was potentially

00:59:20.560 --> 00:59:24.320
dangerous to tell people
about this study, why?

00:59:24.320 --> 00:59:27.360
Well, smoker might think,

00:59:27.360 --> 00:59:29.200
"Why bother quitting smoking?

00:59:29.200 --> 00:59:34.381
My ham and cheese sandwich
is just as bad for me."

00:59:34.381 --> 00:59:36.000
(audience laughing)
So let's not tell anyone about this

00:59:36.000 --> 00:59:38.560
whole meat and cheese thing shhh.

00:59:38.560 --> 00:59:41.520
Reminds me of a famous
Philip Morris cigarette ad

00:59:41.520 --> 00:59:43.600
that tried to downplay the risk by saying,

00:59:43.600 --> 00:59:46.960
"Hey, you think secondhand smoke is bad,

00:59:46.960 --> 00:59:49.200
increasing the risk of lung cancer 19%.

00:59:49.200 --> 00:59:51.920
Well hey, drinking one or two
glasses of milk every day,

00:59:51.920 --> 00:59:55.360
three times as bad, 62%
increased risk of lung cancer."

00:59:55.360 --> 00:59:56.960
Tripling your risk of heart disease

00:59:56.960 --> 00:59:59.040
by eating non-vegetarian.

00:59:59.040 --> 01:00:00.960
Multiplying your risk sixfold if you eat

01:00:00.960 --> 01:00:02.320
lots of meat and dairy.

01:00:02.320 --> 01:00:06.560
So they concluded,

01:00:06.560 --> 01:00:14.541
let's keep some perspective here.

01:00:14.541 --> 01:00:14.560
(audience laughing)

01:00:14.560 --> 01:00:16.960
The risk from secondhand
smoke may be well below that

01:00:16.960 --> 01:00:18.400
of other everyday activities.

01:00:18.400 --> 01:00:24.480
So breathe deep.

01:00:24.480 --> 01:00:24.880
(audience laughing)

01:00:24.880 --> 01:00:27.600
That's like saying it, don't
worry about getting stabbed

01:00:27.600 --> 01:00:32.541
because getting shot so much worse.

01:00:32.541 --> 01:00:32.560
(audience laughing)

01:00:32.560 --> 01:00:38.320
How about neither? Two
risks don't make a right.

01:00:38.320 --> 01:00:40.880
Of course, we'll note Philip
Morris stopped throwing dairy

01:00:40.880 --> 01:00:43.680
under the bus once they
purchased Kraft Foods.

01:00:43.680 --> 01:00:47.360
Just saying.

01:00:47.360 --> 01:00:47.520
(intense music)

01:00:47.520 --> 01:00:51.360
For a while I was thinking,
I mean the insurers,

01:00:51.360 --> 01:00:53.280
you would think the ones, the payers,

01:00:53.280 --> 01:00:55.200
you'd think they'd be clamoring for this

01:00:55.200 --> 01:00:57.680
because it would save them so much money.

01:00:57.680 --> 01:01:01.120
But then you realize they
just get a part of the pie.

01:01:01.120 --> 01:01:04.080
And the bigger the pie,
the more money they make,

01:01:04.080 --> 01:01:06.720
the sicker people are,
the more they spend money,

01:01:06.720 --> 01:01:08.640
the more they can charge for premiums.

01:01:08.640 --> 01:01:11.080
Again, these perverse incentives.

01:01:11.080 --> 01:01:13.440
- Obesity has become very common

01:01:13.440 --> 01:01:15.760
because we are not only eating

01:01:15.760 --> 01:01:17.920
a tremendous amounts of calories,

01:01:17.920 --> 01:01:21.600
way in excess of what our bodies require,

01:01:21.600 --> 01:01:24.080
but the particular combination of sugars

01:01:24.080 --> 01:01:27.360
and fats eaten at the same time

01:01:27.920 --> 01:01:30.240
evokes what's called oxidative priority.

01:01:30.240 --> 01:01:33.040
We burn the sugars and
store the fats for later.

01:01:33.040 --> 01:01:34.960
So when you eat something like ice cream,

01:01:34.960 --> 01:01:36.240
it is fat and sugar.

01:01:36.240 --> 01:01:38.240
You burn the sugar and store the fat.

01:01:38.240 --> 01:01:41.120
When you eat a cheeseburger,
you're gonna burn the sugar

01:01:41.120 --> 01:01:44.000
in the white flour bun and
then the sugar and the ketchup

01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:46.320
and store the fat in
the meat and the cheese.

01:01:46.320 --> 01:01:49.680
So we're eating that sugar fat combination

01:01:49.680 --> 01:01:52.640
pretty much all day from
the bacon and eggs and toast

01:01:52.640 --> 01:01:55.600
in the morning to the
burgers and fries at lunch

01:01:55.600 --> 01:01:59.120
and to the fried chicken and
the milkshake in the evening.

01:01:59.120 --> 01:02:04.800
Even the broiled salmon eaten
with the grilled potatoes

01:02:04.800 --> 01:02:06.800
is that fat and sugar combination.

01:02:06.800 --> 01:02:09.360
So the vast amounts of fat
and sugar that we're eating

01:02:09.360 --> 01:02:13.200
on a daily basis is
making us grossly obese.

01:02:13.200 --> 01:02:15.360
And it's more than just a cosmetic issue

01:02:15.360 --> 01:02:20.160
because as fat accumulates,
especially inside the abdomen,

01:02:20.160 --> 01:02:23.600
intrabdominal fat puts out
on an array of molecules

01:02:23.600 --> 01:02:25.280
that sets off inflammation.

01:02:25.280 --> 01:02:27.680
They're called inflammatory cytokines

01:02:27.680 --> 01:02:31.360
and they set off inflammatory
conditions all over the body.

01:02:31.360 --> 01:02:34.480
So obesity basically is
a state of inflammation.

01:02:34.480 --> 01:02:37.440
People can say, "Well, I'm
obese, but I'm still healthy."

01:02:37.440 --> 01:02:40.400
No, if you're obese, you're
fighting inflammation.

01:02:40.400 --> 01:02:42.640
And that sets the stage for diseases

01:02:42.640 --> 01:02:44.040
in many kinds of organs.

01:02:44.040 --> 01:02:46.160
- Who says that, you know,

01:02:46.160 --> 01:02:49.680
African Americans are
genetically predisposed, not so.

01:02:49.680 --> 01:02:54.800
We have about a 21% higher
cardiovascular mortality rate

01:02:54.800 --> 01:02:57.680
in the black community of this country,

01:02:57.680 --> 01:03:00.160
and it really does have
to do with the diet.

01:03:00.160 --> 01:03:02.720
It was called out by the
Regards Trial investigators.

01:03:02.720 --> 01:03:05.200
Anyone can look that
up to the Regards Trial

01:03:05.200 --> 01:03:08.880
and you'll see these publications
that say the Southern diet

01:03:08.880 --> 01:03:11.600
and what they really mean
by that, the soul food.

01:03:11.600 --> 01:03:14.160
It's taking your greens and
putting ham hocks in it,

01:03:14.160 --> 01:03:17.520
or taking the yams and
making candy yams out of it.

01:03:17.520 --> 01:03:19.920
So more cholesterol, more saturated fat,

01:03:19.920 --> 01:03:21.680
not just chicken, but fried chicken.

01:03:21.680 --> 01:03:24.080
And if you have that sodium content,

01:03:24.080 --> 01:03:26.560
the cholesterol content,
saturated fat and sodium

01:03:26.560 --> 01:03:29.280
with sugar, that's a
combination that is set up

01:03:29.280 --> 01:03:34.863
for heart disease, kidney
disease, stroke, and death.

01:03:34.863 --> 01:03:37.840
(intense music)
- Each year you are reborn.

01:03:37.840 --> 01:03:40.960
You create and destroy nearly
your entire body weight

01:03:40.960 --> 01:03:44.320
in new cells every year.

01:03:44.320 --> 01:03:46.880
Your cells are pre-programmed
to die naturally,

01:03:46.880 --> 01:03:49.200
to make way for fresh cells.

01:03:49.200 --> 01:03:52.640
In a sense, your body's
rebuilding itself every few months

01:03:52.640 --> 01:03:57.440
with the building materials
you provided through your diet.

01:03:57.440 --> 01:04:00.640
Some cells, however,
overstay their welcome,

01:04:00.640 --> 01:04:03.200
namely cancer cells.

01:04:03.200 --> 01:04:06.080
By somehow disabling their
own suicide mechanisms,

01:04:06.080 --> 01:04:08.640
they don't die when they're supposed to.

01:04:08.640 --> 01:04:10.880
Because they continue
to thrive and divide,

01:04:10.880 --> 01:04:12.640
cancer cells can eventually form tumors

01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:15.600
and potentially spread
throughout the body.

01:04:16.560 --> 01:04:19.120
All cells contain
so-called death receptors

01:04:19.120 --> 01:04:21.840
that trigger the
self-destruction sequence.

01:04:21.840 --> 01:04:25.120
But cancer cells can disable
their own death receptors.

01:04:25.120 --> 01:04:26.960
Vegetables are selective.

01:04:26.960 --> 01:04:30.400
They destroy cancer cells,
but leave normal cells alone

01:04:30.400 --> 01:04:32.640
and underscores the
importance of including

01:04:32.640 --> 01:04:39.583
a variety of vegetables in your diet.

01:04:39.583 --> 01:04:42.960
(intense music)
- What is the science of the disease?

01:04:42.960 --> 01:04:46.480
And by that I mean the following,

01:04:46.480 --> 01:04:47.760
if we can have them understand

01:04:47.760 --> 01:04:50.720
that all experts in
this disease would agree

01:04:50.720 --> 01:04:52.480
that where cardiovascular disease

01:04:52.480 --> 01:04:55.920
has its inception, its
onset, its beginning,

01:04:55.920 --> 01:04:59.120
is when we progressively
injure the life jacket

01:04:59.120 --> 01:05:00.800
and the guardian of our blood vessels,

01:05:00.800 --> 01:05:04.480
which happens to be that
delicate innermost lining,

01:05:04.480 --> 01:05:06.880
the endothelium.

01:05:06.880 --> 01:05:09.680
And what truly makes the
endothelium so magical

01:05:09.680 --> 01:05:13.920
is the molecule of gas, nitric
oxide, that it produces,

01:05:13.920 --> 01:05:16.000
which is the great protector

01:05:16.000 --> 01:05:18.320
and salvation of all of our blood vessels

01:05:18.320 --> 01:05:20.000
because of its remarkable functions.

01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:23.680
For example, nitric oxide
will keep all the cellular

01:05:23.680 --> 01:05:25.840
elements within our
bloodstream flowing smoothly

01:05:25.840 --> 01:05:28.000
like Teflon rather than Velcro.

01:05:28.000 --> 01:05:31.120
Number two, nitric oxide is

01:05:31.120 --> 01:05:33.280
the strongest blood vessel
dilator in the body.

01:05:33.280 --> 01:05:35.520
When you climb stairs, the
arteries to your heart,

01:05:35.520 --> 01:05:37.360
to your legs, they widen, they dilate.

01:05:37.360 --> 01:05:38.480
That's nitric oxide.

01:05:38.480 --> 01:05:43.600
Number three, nitric oxide
keeps the wall of the artery

01:05:43.600 --> 01:05:45.680
from becoming thick and stiff or inflamed.

01:05:45.680 --> 01:05:49.520
Protects us from getting high
blood pressure, hypertension.

01:05:49.520 --> 01:05:53.440
Number four, and this is the absolute key.

01:05:53.440 --> 01:05:58.480
Number four, a safe and
normal amount of nitric oxide

01:05:58.480 --> 01:06:00.000
will protect us all

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.480
from ever developing blockages or plaque.

01:06:03.440 --> 01:06:08.000
However, anybody who develops
cardiovascular disease,

01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:12.000
whether they're in New York,
Chicago, London, Berlin,

01:06:12.000 --> 01:06:13.920
is because in the previous decades,

01:06:13.920 --> 01:06:18.640
they now have so sufficiently
trashed, injured, compromised,

01:06:18.640 --> 01:06:22.080
and turned their endothelial
system into a train wreck.

01:06:22.080 --> 01:06:24.880
They no no longer have enough nitric oxide

01:06:24.880 --> 01:06:30.160
to protect themselves from
making blockages and plaque.

01:06:31.280 --> 01:06:34.800
But the good news here is this,

01:06:34.800 --> 01:06:37.280
this is not a malignancy.

01:06:37.280 --> 01:06:40.560
And once you get patients
to stop ever again

01:06:40.560 --> 01:06:42.880
passing any morsel through their lips,

01:06:42.880 --> 01:06:44.400
it is going to further destroy

01:06:44.400 --> 01:06:47.360
an already train wrecked endothelium.

01:06:47.360 --> 01:06:50.800
Then rapidly the endothelial,
the system recovers,

01:06:50.800 --> 01:06:52.320
makes enough nitric oxide.

01:06:52.320 --> 01:06:54.800
So, you know, not only
can you halt the disease,

01:06:54.800 --> 01:06:57.280
but often we'll see significant elements

01:06:57.280 --> 01:06:59.200
of disease reversal.

01:06:59.200 --> 01:07:05.120
- Any lifestyle medicine
doctor can tell you this,

01:07:05.120 --> 01:07:07.120
is where all of a sudden
people get better.

01:07:07.120 --> 01:07:08.720
In fact, it's interesting when I go

01:07:08.720 --> 01:07:10.480
to these lifestyle medicine conferences

01:07:10.480 --> 01:07:12.240
and talk to my fellow physicians

01:07:12.240 --> 01:07:14.640
and I ask them the question, which is,

01:07:14.640 --> 01:07:16.000
how did you get into this?

01:07:16.000 --> 01:07:18.720
Like, you know, I mean,
none of us were taught this

01:07:18.720 --> 01:07:19.680
in medical school.

01:07:19.680 --> 01:07:20.720
So why are you here?

01:07:20.720 --> 01:07:24.880
Like, what was the light bulb moment?

01:07:24.880 --> 01:07:26.400
'Cause of course, I
wanna find out what it is

01:07:26.400 --> 01:07:28.880
so I can tell the rest of my colleagues.

01:07:28.880 --> 01:07:32.160
And you know, more often
than not, it's a patient.

01:07:32.160 --> 01:07:34.080
It's a patient that educated them.

01:07:34.080 --> 01:07:35.360
All of a sudden, one of the patients

01:07:35.360 --> 01:07:37.920
that's been coming to them for years,

01:07:37.920 --> 01:07:39.760
all of a sudden they look great.

01:07:39.760 --> 01:07:41.040
They lost all this weight.

01:07:41.840 --> 01:07:43.040
In fact, they probably came to them

01:07:43.040 --> 01:07:44.640
because all of a sudden their
blood pressure's too low,

01:07:44.640 --> 01:07:47.600
they're overmedicated
and said, "Wait a second.

01:07:47.600 --> 01:07:50.480
I've been following you and
your family for all these years.

01:07:50.480 --> 01:07:51.520
What happened?"

01:07:51.520 --> 01:07:54.320
You know, and they're like,
"Oh, I read the China Study,

01:07:54.320 --> 01:07:56.640
or I saw, you know, 'Forks over Knives,'"

01:07:56.640 --> 01:07:59.440
or they got a hold of some resource

01:07:59.440 --> 01:08:01.440
and then change their whole lives,

01:08:01.440 --> 01:08:02.720
change the lives of their family

01:08:02.720 --> 01:08:05.920
and their doctors just spell
bound thinking to themselves,

01:08:05.920 --> 01:08:06.640
in the back of their mind.

01:08:06.640 --> 01:08:09.040
"Wait a second, I've got
like thousands of patients

01:08:09.040 --> 01:08:10.080
just like you."

01:08:10.080 --> 01:08:12.160
- You know, half to two thirds of people

01:08:12.160 --> 01:08:14.160
prescribed cholesterol or
drugs aren't taking them

01:08:14.160 --> 01:08:15.920
after just four to six months,

01:08:15.920 --> 01:08:17.600
even though they're proven value in people

01:08:17.600 --> 01:08:19.280
who have heart disease.

01:08:19.280 --> 01:08:21.600
But when paradoxically, you know,

01:08:21.600 --> 01:08:23.760
Medicare has been covering
my lifestyle program

01:08:23.760 --> 01:08:25.200
for reversing heart disease.

01:08:25.200 --> 01:08:26.880
And most of the major insurance companies

01:08:26.880 --> 01:08:28.000
are now doing that.

01:08:28.000 --> 01:08:29.680
And we've been training
hospitals and clinics

01:08:29.680 --> 01:08:31.600
and physician groups around the country,

01:08:31.600 --> 01:08:34.000
and we're getting bigger
changes in lifestyle,

01:08:34.000 --> 01:08:36.560
better clinical outcomes,
bigger cost savings,

01:08:36.560 --> 01:08:38.440
and better adherence
than anyone's ever shown.

01:08:38.440 --> 01:08:42.320
- This is nature. This
is a fact of nature.

01:08:42.320 --> 01:08:47.680
What we're discovering, once
again, is how nature works.

01:08:47.680 --> 01:08:53.040
And that's what goes on
inside of a cell, one cell.

01:08:53.040 --> 01:08:54.400
And we have some people actually

01:08:54.400 --> 01:08:57.440
maybe between 10 and a hundred
trillion cells in a body,

01:08:57.440 --> 01:09:00.800
and each of them doing their own thing.

01:09:00.800 --> 01:09:04.960
This is all operating in a symphonic way.

01:09:04.960 --> 01:09:06.880
Once you get to this point of realization,

01:09:06.880 --> 01:09:08.800
you get this kind of empirical data.

01:09:08.800 --> 01:09:13.120
You cannot argue, "Oh, it's
the other way around." No.

01:09:13.120 --> 01:09:15.120
- Alright, high blood pressure,

01:09:15.120 --> 01:09:17.440
78 million Americans affected.

01:09:17.440 --> 01:09:19.360
That's one in three American adults.

01:09:19.360 --> 01:09:21.520
As we get older, pressures
get higher and higher.

01:09:21.520 --> 01:09:26.000
(indistinct) age 60, most of
us have high blood pressure.

01:09:26.000 --> 01:09:26.880
So wait a second.

01:09:26.880 --> 01:09:29.280
If most of us get hypertension, well,

01:09:29.280 --> 01:09:33.520
maybe it's just a natural
inevitable consequence of aging.

01:09:33.520 --> 01:09:35.680
No, we've noticed since the 1920s,

01:09:35.680 --> 01:09:37.520
high blood pressure need not occur.

01:09:37.520 --> 01:09:39.200
Researchers measured the blood pressures

01:09:39.200 --> 01:09:41.520
of a thousand people
living in rural Kenya.

01:09:41.520 --> 01:09:44.480
Typical Kenyan diets, something like this.

01:09:44.480 --> 01:09:47.120
Corn, beans, vegetable, fruit, greens.

01:09:47.120 --> 01:09:51.440
Our pressures go up as we
age, such that by age 60,

01:09:51.440 --> 01:09:53.280
most of us have high blood pressure.

01:09:53.280 --> 01:09:57.440
Their pressures go down

01:09:57.440 --> 01:10:00.560
and the lower the better.

01:10:00.560 --> 01:10:04.320
So 140 over 90 cutoff is arbitrary.

01:10:04.320 --> 01:10:07.760
I mean, even people with
pressures under 120 over 80

01:10:07.760 --> 01:10:10.000
may benefit from blood pressure reduction.

01:10:10.000 --> 01:10:12.960
So the ideal blood pressure,

01:10:12.960 --> 01:10:16.640
the no benefit from reducing
it further blood pressure

01:10:16.640 --> 01:10:20.400
110 over 70.

01:10:21.040 --> 01:10:24.720
Is it even possible to get
pressures down to 110 over 70?

01:10:24.720 --> 01:10:26.160
It's not just possible.

01:10:26.160 --> 01:10:32.560
It's normal for those
living healthy enough lives.

01:10:32.560 --> 01:10:34.320
Two years of this rural Kenyan hospital,

01:10:34.320 --> 01:10:35.920
1800 patients were admitted.

01:10:35.920 --> 01:10:39.280
How many cases of high blood
pressure did they find? Zero.

01:10:39.840 --> 01:10:42.640
Wow. Must have had low rates
of heart disease, right?

01:10:42.640 --> 01:10:44.640
No, they had no rates of heart disease.

01:10:44.640 --> 01:10:46.400
Now, the single case of arteriosclerosis,

01:10:46.400 --> 01:10:49.680
our number one killer was found.

01:10:49.680 --> 01:10:52.000
Rural China, same thing.

01:10:52.000 --> 01:10:54.480
About 110 over 70 their entire lives.

01:10:54.480 --> 01:10:59.360
70 year olds with same blood
pressure as 16 year olds.

01:10:59.360 --> 01:11:02.240
It's amazing in Asia, Africa,
vastly different diets.

01:11:02.240 --> 01:11:05.680
What they shared in common
is that they're plant-based

01:11:05.680 --> 01:11:08.560
day to day with meat only
eaten on special occasions.

01:11:09.200 --> 01:11:11.360
It's amazing, why do we think
is the plant-based nature

01:11:11.360 --> 01:11:13.360
of their diets that was so protective?

01:11:13.360 --> 01:11:15.440
Because in the western world,

01:11:15.440 --> 01:11:17.040
according to American Heart Association,

01:11:17.040 --> 01:11:19.440
the only group of folks
getting it down to that low

01:11:19.440 --> 01:11:25.200
on average, are those eating
strictly plant-based diets,

01:11:25.200 --> 01:11:30.560
coming in at a perfect 110 over 65.

01:11:31.520 --> 01:11:34.160
This is the largest group of largest study

01:11:34.160 --> 01:11:36.320
of plant-based eaters in history

01:11:36.320 --> 01:11:40.880
following 89,000 Californians,
comparing non-vegetarians

01:11:40.880 --> 01:11:42.560
to so-called semi vegetarians,

01:11:42.560 --> 01:11:45.600
those who eat meat more on a
weekly basis than a daily basis

01:11:45.600 --> 01:11:48.560
compared to those who
eat no meat except fish,

01:11:48.560 --> 01:11:50.800
compared to those who eat no meat at all,

01:11:50.800 --> 01:11:53.600
compared to those who eat
no meat, eggs, or dairy.

01:11:53.600 --> 01:11:55.280
And this was an Adventist study,

01:11:55.280 --> 01:11:58.240
so even the non-vegetarians
didn't eat a lot of meat

01:11:58.240 --> 01:11:59.680
compared to the general population.

01:11:59.680 --> 01:12:00.960
Ate lots of fruits and vegetables,

01:12:00.960 --> 01:12:02.960
tend not to smoke, and exercise.

01:12:02.960 --> 01:12:06.960
This is a really healthy
group of meat eaters.

01:12:06.960 --> 01:12:10.880
But still we see this
kind of stepwise drop

01:12:10.880 --> 01:12:12.240
in high blood pressure rates

01:12:12.240 --> 01:12:14.720
the more and more plant-based people ate.

01:12:14.720 --> 01:12:18.640
Same thing with diabetes,
same thing with obesity.

01:12:18.640 --> 01:12:20.640
You can show this experimentally.

01:12:20.640 --> 01:12:22.800
You take vegetarians, you give them meat,

01:12:22.800 --> 01:12:26.160
pay them enough to eat it, and
their blood pressures go up.

01:12:26.160 --> 01:12:28.160
Or you take people who already eat meat,

01:12:28.160 --> 01:12:29.440
remove meat from their diet

01:12:29.440 --> 01:12:32.640
and their blood pressures
go down within seven days.

01:12:32.640 --> 01:12:34.320
And this is after the vast majority

01:12:34.320 --> 01:12:37.680
had to stop their medications
or reduce their medications.

01:12:37.680 --> 01:12:39.200
They had to stop the medications.

01:12:39.200 --> 01:12:41.840
I mean, if you treat the
cause, eliminate the disease,

01:12:41.840 --> 01:12:43.760
you can't be on multiple
blood pressure medications

01:12:43.760 --> 01:12:44.720
with normal blood pressure.

01:12:44.720 --> 01:12:47.760
You drop your pressures too
low, get dizzy, fall over,

01:12:47.760 --> 01:12:48.640
hurt yourself.

01:12:48.640 --> 01:12:52.160
Lower pressures your doctor
has to pull you off the pills.

01:12:52.160 --> 01:12:55.600
Lower pressures on fewer drugs.

01:12:55.600 --> 01:13:01.663
That's the power of plants.

01:13:01.663 --> 01:13:04.400
(intense music)
- We've had about a 70% decrease

01:13:04.400 --> 01:13:06.160
in cardiovascular mortality

01:13:06.160 --> 01:13:07.680
just the time that I've been, you know,

01:13:07.680 --> 01:13:10.240
from the time I went to
medical school until now.

01:13:10.240 --> 01:13:14.880
And it was really a lot of thoughtful,

01:13:14.880 --> 01:13:18.080
hardworking, dedicated physicians.

01:13:18.080 --> 01:13:20.560
Andreas Gruentzig, coming
up with angioplasty,

01:13:20.560 --> 01:13:22.240
which then became stenting.

01:13:22.240 --> 01:13:26.000
We had people developing bypass
surgery, heart transplants,

01:13:26.000 --> 01:13:30.560
you know, putting in defibrillators,
coming up with statins,

01:13:30.560 --> 01:13:32.960
ALLHAT, the hypertension program

01:13:32.960 --> 01:13:34.320
that really changed the paradigm

01:13:34.320 --> 01:13:36.320
for how we treat blood pressure.

01:13:36.320 --> 01:13:38.800
All of these things, all
these dedicated physicians,

01:13:38.800 --> 01:13:40.560
all of this career that they dedicated

01:13:40.560 --> 01:13:43.200
lose to a double cheeseburger, really?

01:13:43.200 --> 01:13:44.480
That's really what's going on

01:13:44.480 --> 01:13:48.400
and our CDC, Center for Disease Control,

01:13:48.400 --> 01:13:50.400
is talking about it incessantly.

01:13:50.400 --> 01:13:52.640
That our Medicare system
is gonna go broke,

01:13:52.640 --> 01:13:54.400
if we don't change something,

01:13:54.400 --> 01:13:57.200
and that mortality that we fought so hard

01:13:57.200 --> 01:13:59.520
to get down is headed right back up.

01:13:59.520 --> 01:14:01.360
So what are we gonna do about it?

01:14:01.360 --> 01:14:04.000
I'm telling everybody
it's their patriotic duty

01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:05.680
to do a whole food plant-based diet

01:14:05.680 --> 01:14:09.983
and tell everybody about it.

01:14:09.983 --> 01:14:11.280
(intense music)
- You know, a few years ago,

01:14:11.280 --> 01:14:12.960
Dr. Kim Williams became president

01:14:12.960 --> 01:14:15.600
of the American College of Cardiology.

01:14:15.600 --> 01:14:18.400
He was asked in an
interview why he himself

01:14:18.400 --> 01:14:20.480
follows the same diet he
recommends to all his patients,

01:14:20.480 --> 01:14:22.000
strictly plant-based diet.

01:14:22.000 --> 01:14:25.520
"I don't mind dying,"
Dr. Williams replied,

01:14:25.520 --> 01:14:31.261
"I just don't want it to be my own fault."

01:14:31.261 --> 01:14:32.927
(audience laughing)
Thank you so much, everyone.

